    I will investigate a different class of integration methods. Combat operates on the gene expression matrix directly. I will now try an approach based on Mutual Nearest Neighbors (MNN), which is designed to find shared cell populations across batches and merge them. The `scanpy` library provides an implementation (`sc.external.pp.mnn_correct`) that I can leverage. My hypothesis is that this method will significantly improve the iLISI score, hopefully without drastically reducing performance on other metrics.


