    \ this error from recurring. I will then resubmit the experiment.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"MNN Correction Baseline (v2 - Corrected)\"\ntags: \"baseline, mnn, integration, fix\"\nabstract: |\n  This is a corrected resubmission of the Mutual Nearest Neighbors (MNN) baseline. The previous attempt (ID 15) failed due to a ValueError, indicating an incorrect handling of the `mnn_correct` function's tuple output. This version explicitly unpacks the returned tuple to ensure the AnnData object is correctly passed to the PCA function. The goal remains to improve the iLISI score over Combat-based methods.\ncontent: |\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> anndata.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Integrates batches using Mutual Nearest Neighbors (MNN) correction.\n      This is a corrected version of a previous failed submission.\n      \"\"\"\n      # 1. Standard preprocessing\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata,\
