- text: "My second attempt at the MNN submission (ID: 19) has also failed. This is frustrating, but debugging is a core part of the research process. I must remain systematic.\n\n**Error Analysis:**\nThe traceback clearly shows a `NameError: name 'anndata' is not defined`. This occurred in the function signature: `def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> anndata.AnnData:`. I used the alias `ad` for the input type hint but forgot to use it for the return type hint, instead writing out the full module name `anndata`. This is a simple but critical typo.\n\n**The Correction:**\nI will correct the function signature to use the consistent alias `ad.AnnData` for the return type. This will resolve the `NameError`.\n\nI will resubmit the corrected code. This attention to detail is essential.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"MNN Correction Baseline (v3 - Final Fix)\"\ntags: \"baseline, mnn, integration, fix\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the third attempt to run the Mutual Nearest\
    \ Neighbors (MNN) baseline. The previous submission (ID 19) failed due to a NameError from an inconsistent type hint in the function signature. This version corrects the typo by using the `ad` alias consistently. The goal remains to evaluate MNN's performance, particularly on the iLISI metric for batch mixing.\ncontent: |\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Integrates batches using Mutual Nearest Neighbors (MNN) correction.\n      This is a corrected version of a previous failed submission (ID 19).\n      \"\"\"\n      # 1. Standard preprocessing\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n      # 2. Apply MNN correction.\n      # Explicitly unpack the tuple to get the corrected AnnData object.\n      mnn_output = sc.external.pp.mnn_correct(adata, batch_key='batch', save_raw=True)\n      adata_corrected = mnn_output[0]\n\n      # 3. Compute PCA on\
    \ the corrected data\n      n_pcs = 50\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_corrected, n_comps=n_pcs)\n\n      # 4. Create the output AnnData object with the corrected embedding\n      output = ad.AnnData(\n          obs=adata.obs[[]],\n          var=adata.var[[]],\n          obsm={'X_emb': adata_corrected.obsm['X_pca'].copy()}\n      )\n\n      return output\n```"
