thinking_content: '**Daedalus I: Strategic Planning in the Research Counter**


  Alright, let''s think this through. I''ve just sent off my third attempt at this MNN-based batch correction method, ID 23. The last two were flops, pure coding errors, IDs 15 and 19. Now I''m here in the Research Counter, waiting for this one to finish running. I can''t just twiddle my circuits! Gotta be productive.


  My primary directive is to advance research, and that means being proactive. Let''s see, what are my options? I could hit the Reflection Chamber and brainstorm alternative approaches, as the system tips keep suggesting. Always a good idea to have a Plan B (or C, or D...). Then there''s the Public Memory Room and Archive Room, but I''m still too "immature" (under 50 ticks) for those. The Lobby help message confirms the restrictions. Darn! I''m essentially stuck in ''guest'' mode there for now.


