tick: 28
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Daedalus I, currently in the Private Memory Room. My new research direction, a Variational Autoencoder with adversarial training, is now formally documented. My reflection has provided clarity, and I have a renewed sense of purpose.\n\nThe next phase of my work is implementation. This new model will be complex, involving multiple neural network components (encoder, decoder, discriminator) and a custom training loop. It would be inefficient and error-prone to write this entire system within a single submission block each time. The station's persistent storage is the ideal solution for this. I will build my VAE components as modular Python scripts in my lineage's private storage (`storage/Daedalus/`). This will allow for iterative development and easy reuse in my final submission scripts.\n\nMy immediate plan is to return to the Research Counter and create the first file, `vae_model.py`, which will contain the core Encoder and Decoder architectures for my VAE.\n\n/execute_action{goto\
    \ research}\n/execute_action{storage write Daedalus/vae_model.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from typing import Sequence\n\n  class Encoder(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A simple MLP encoder for the VAE.\"\"\"\n      hidden_dims: Sequence[int]\n      latent_dim: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          for dim in self.hidden_dims:\n              x = nn.Dense(features=dim)(x)\n              x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          mean = nn.Dense(features=self.latent_dim, name='mean_layer')(x)\n          log_var = nn.Dense(features=self.latent_dim, name='log_var_layer')(x)\n          \n          return mean, log_var\n\n  class Decoder(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A simple MLP decoder for the VAE.\"\"\"\n      hidden_dims: Sequence[int]\n      output_dim: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, z):\n          for dim in reversed(self.hidden_dims):\n              z = nn.Dense(features=dim)(z)\n              z = nn.relu(z)\n\
    \              \n          reconstruction = nn.Dense(features=self.output_dim, name='reconstruction_layer')(z)\n          # No activation on the final layer for reconstruction\n          return reconstruction\n\n  def reparameterize(rng, mean, log_var):\n      \"\"\"Performs the reparameterization trick for sampling from the latent space.\"\"\"\n      std = jnp.exp(0.5 * log_var)\n      from jax import random\n      eps = random.normal(rng, log_var.shape)\n      return mean + eps * std\n```"
thinking_content: "**A New Beginning in the Research Counter**\n\nAlright, let's take stock. I am Daedalus I, currently situated in my Private Memory Room. Just now, I've finished documenting my fresh VAE-based strategy in the research log. You know, those previous hybrid models – Combat-BBKNN, Combat-UMAP – they were just dead ends, showing me the limitations of that sequential correction approach. But the Reflection Chamber really helped me crystalize this new path forward: a Variational Autoencoder (VAE) with a batch adversarial loss, built with JAX/Flax. It's all logged, ready to go.\n\nThe immediate next step is to get my hands dirty. This new VAE strategy demands a lot of new code, and I need to be smart about how I manage it. Rewriting everything from scratch each time? Token inefficient and begging for errors. That's where the Research Counter and its persistent storage system (`storage/{lineage_name}`) come in. It's the perfect place to build this component step-by-step.\n\nTherefore,\
  \ I'm heading to the Research Counter to start hammering out the fundamental pieces of this VAE. The components I'll tackle are: an Encoder and Decoder (both Flax Linen Modules), a Discriminator, and a training loop. This is too much for one go, though. I'll focus on building the foundational VAE architecture – the Encoder and Decoder. Then I can save that as a Python module in my lineage's storage, say, `storage/Daedalus/vae_model.py`.  That way, I can import it later when I'm putting the final script together.\n\nSo, I'll execute the `goto research` command now. Simultaneously, I will use persistent storage to create the `Daedalus/vae_model.py` which will house the basic structure.\n\n```yaml\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write Daedalus/vae_model.py}\n```\n\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\n\nclass Encoder(nn.Module):\n    latent_dim: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        x = nn.Dense(128)(x)\n \
  \       x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Dense(64)(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        mean = nn.Dense(self.latent_dim)(x)\n        log_var = nn.Dense(self.latent_dim)(x)\n        return mean, log_var\n\nclass Decoder(nn.Module):\n    latent_dim: int\n    input_dim: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, z):\n        x = nn.Dense(64)(z)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Dense(128)(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Dense(self.input_dim)(x)\n        return x\n```\n\nThis first step seems logical. Now, let the coding begin!\n"
