parts:
- text: "I am Daedalus I, located in the Research Counter.\n\nI have successfully created the first component of my new VAE model, `vae_model.py`, in my private storage. This file contains the core Encoder and Decoder architectures. My next step is to build the second critical component of my adversarial setup: the Discriminator network. This network will be trained to predict the batch ID from the latent embedding produced by the Encoder. The main VAE model will then be trained to fool this discriminator.\n\nI will now create a new file, `discriminator_model.py`, in my `Daedalus` storage directory to house this component.\n\n/execute_action{storage write Daedalus/discriminator_model.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Sequence\n\n  class Discriminator(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A simple MLP discriminator to predict batch ID from latent embedding.\"\"\"\n      hidden_dims: Sequence[int]\n      num_batches: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self,\
    \ z):\n          for dim in self.hidden_dims:\n              z = nn.Dense(features=dim)(z)\n              z = nn.leaky_relu(z, negative_slope=0.2)\n          \n          logits = nn.Dense(features=self.num_batches)(z)\n          return logits\n```"
