tick: 31
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Daedalus I, in the Research Counter.\n\nI have now created all the necessary modular components for my Adversarial VAE model: the VAE architecture, the discriminator, and the core training logic. They are safely stored in my private lineage storage. With this preparatory work complete, I am finally ready to assemble them into a single, executable script and submit my first experiment based on this new research direction.\n\nThis submission will import the modules I have created, initialize the models and training states, run the adversarial training loop for a set number of epochs, and finally, generate the batch-corrected embedding from the trained encoder. This is the culmination of my reflection and development over the last several ticks.\n\nI will now submit this first version of my Adversarial VAE.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Adversarial VAE for Batch Integration (v1)\"\ntags: \"vae, adversarial, deep-learning, jax, flax, generative\"\nabstract: |\n\
    \  This submission introduces a novel, first-principles approach to batch integration using a Variational Autoencoder (VAE) with an adversarial training objective. \n  The model consists of a VAE (encoder/decoder) and a discriminator network. The VAE is trained to reconstruct the gene expression profile while its latent embedding is simultaneously trained to fool the discriminator, which tries to predict the batch of origin.\n  This forces the model to learn a batch-invariant representation. The final output is the mean of the latent space embedding from the trained encoder.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/Daedalus')\n\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from flax.training import train_state\n  import optax\n  from tqdm import tqdm\n\n  # Import modular components from storage\n  from vae_model import Encoder, Decoder, reparameterize\n  from discriminator_model import Discriminator\n\
    \  from training_logic import VAETrainState, train_step\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Trains an adversarial VAE to learn a batch-invariant embedding.\n      \"\"\"\n      # --- 1. Data Preprocessing ---\n      print(\"Step 1: Preprocessing data...\")\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      \n      data = adata.X.toarray() if hasattr(adata.X, 'toarray') else adata.X\n      batch_info = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n      batch_labels = batch_info.cat.codes.to_numpy()\n      num_batches = len(batch_info.cat.categories)\n\n      # --- 2. Model and State Initialization ---\n      print(\"Step 2: Initializing models and training states...\")\n      rng = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n      rng, vae_key, disc_key = jax.random.split(rng, 3)\n      \n      # Model parameters\n      input_dim = data.shape[1]\n      latent_dim = 32\n      encoder_dims = [512, 256]\n      decoder_dims = [256,\
    \ 512]\n      discriminator_dims = [128, 64]\n      learning_rate = 1e-4\n\n      # Init VAE\n      encoder = Encoder(hidden_dims=encoder_dims, latent_dim=latent_dim)\n      decoder = Decoder(hidden_dims=decoder_dims, output_dim=input_dim)\n      \n      encoder_params = encoder.init(vae_key, jnp.ones((1, input_dim)))['params']\n      decoder_params = decoder.init(vae_key, jnp.ones((1, latent_dim)))['params']\n      \n      # Init Discriminator\n      discriminator = Discriminator(hidden_dims=discriminator_dims, num_batches=num_batches)\n      disc_params = discriminator.init(disc_key, jnp.ones((1, latent_dim)))['params']\n\n      # Create Train States\n      vae_tx = optax.adam(learning_rate)\n      disc_tx = optax.adam(learning_rate)\n      \n      vae_state = VAETrainState.create(\n          apply_fn={'encoder': encoder.apply, 'decoder': decoder.apply},\n          params=None, # Not used directly, params stored in encoder/decoder_params\n          tx=vae_tx,\n          encoder_params=encoder_params,\n\
    \          decoder_params=decoder_params\n      )\n      \n      disc_state = train_state.TrainState.create(\n          apply_fn=discriminator.apply,\n          params=disc_params,\n          tx=disc_tx\n      )\n\n      # --- 3. Training Loop ---\n      print(\"Step 3: Starting adversarial training loop...\")\n      num_epochs = 50\n      batch_size = 512\n      kl_weight = 0.005\n      adv_weight = 0.5\n      \n      num_steps = data.shape[0] // batch_size\n      \n      for epoch in range(num_epochs):\n          rng, epoch_rng = jax.random.split(rng)\n          perms = jax.random.permutation(epoch_rng, data.shape[0])\n          data_perm = data[perms, :]\n          labels_perm = batch_labels[perms]\n          \n          epoch_metrics = []\n          for i in range(num_steps):\n              batch_idx = i * batch_size\n              batch_data = data_perm[batch_idx : batch_idx + batch_size]\n              batch_lbls = labels_perm[batch_idx : batch_idx + batch_size]\n             \
    \ \n              rng, step_rng = jax.random.split(rng)\n              vae_state, disc_state, metrics = train_step(\n                  step_rng, vae_state, disc_state, batch_data, batch_lbls, kl_weight, adv_weight\n              )\n              epoch_metrics.append(metrics)\n          \n          # Log metrics for the epoch\n          avg_metrics = {k: jnp.mean(jnp.array([m[k] for m in epoch_metrics])) for k in epoch_metrics[0]}\n          print(f\"Epoch {epoch+1}/{num_epochs} - VAE Loss: {avg_metrics['total_vae_loss']:.4f}, Disc Loss: {avg_metrics['discriminator_loss']:.4f}\")\n\n      # --- 4. Generate Final Embedding ---\n      print(\"Step 4: Generating final embedding...\")\n      final_embedding, _ = encoder.apply({'params': vae_state.encoder_params}, data)\n\n      # --- 5. Create Output ---\n      print(\"Step 5: Finalizing output...\")\n      output = ad.AnnData(\n          obs=adata.obs[[]],\n          var=adata.var[[]],\n          obsm={'X_emb': jax.device_get(final_embedding)}\n\
    \      )\n\n      return output\n```"
