tick: 33
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 33\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Daedalus I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on achieving novel breakthroughs through systematic research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 73,183 / 300,000 used (24%)\n- Agent Age: 33 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Adversarial VAE for Batch Integration (v1)' (ID: 68) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.4760557819459434\n**ASW_batch:** 0.420\n**ASW_label:** 0.171\n**ARI:** 0.552\n**NMI:** 0.614\n**Graph_conn:** 0.779\n**kBET:** 0.770\n**iLISI:** 0.095\n**cLISI:** 0.938\n**PCR:** 0.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.422\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.420  ASW_label: 0.171  ARI: 0.552  NMI: 0.614\n  Graph_conn: 0.779  kBET: 0.770  iLISI: 0.095  cLISI: 0.938\n  PCR: 0.000  Cell_cycle: 0.422\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch:\
    \ 0.722770  ASW_label: 0.510526  ARI: 0.551538  NMI: 0.613685\n  Graph_conn: 0.782616  kBET: 0.735173  iLISI: 0.094751  cLISI: 0.982014\n  PCR: 0.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.368530\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 68\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the submission and achieved a score of 0.476. The code now runs without crashing and completes all 50 training epochs.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had two critical bugs:\n\n1. **GPU/CUDA Error**: JAX was trying to use CUDA/GPU by default, but no GPU was available in the evaluation environment, causing:\n   ```\n   RuntimeError: Unable to initialize backend 'cuda': FAILED_PRECONDITION: No visible GPU devices.\n   ```\n\n2. **Missing VAETrainState.apply_gradients() Implementation**: The custom `VAETrainState` class in `storage/daedalus/training_logic.py` was missing a proper `apply_gradients()` method to handle the split encoder/decoder parameter structure. The standard Flax `TrainState.apply_gradients()` doesn't\
    \ know how to handle the custom `encoder_params` and `decoder_params` fields.\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n### Fix 1: Force JAX to Use CPU\nAdded at the very beginning of the script (before JAX imports):\n```python\nimport os\nos.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'\n```\n\n### Fix 2: Implement Custom apply_gradients() Method\nCopied the buggy `VAETrainState` class from the lineage directory and added a proper `apply_gradients()` implementation:\n\n```python\nclass VAETrainState(train_state.TrainState):\n    \"\"\"A TrainState for the VAE, holding encoder and decoder params.\"\"\"\n    encoder_params: Any\n    decoder_params: Any\n\n    def apply_gradients(self, *, grads, **kwargs):\n        \"\"\"Apply gradients to encoder and decoder params separately.\"\"\"\n        # Create a params structure that matches the grads structure\n        params_tree = {\n            'encoder_params': self.encoder_params,\n            'decoder_params': self.decoder_params\n        }\n\n        updates, new_opt_state\
    \ = self.tx.update(\n            grads, self.opt_state, params_tree\n        )\n\n        # Apply updates to encoder and decoder params\n        new_encoder_params = optax.apply_updates(self.encoder_params, updates['encoder_params'])\n        new_decoder_params = optax.apply_updates(self.decoder_params, updates['decoder_params'])\n\n        return self.replace(\n            step=self.step + 1,\n            encoder_params=new_encoder_params,\n            decoder_params=new_decoder_params,\n            opt_state=new_opt_state,\n            **kwargs,\n        )\n```\n\nAlso updated the state creation to pass the combined params structure:\n```python\ncombined_params = {\n    'encoder_params': encoder_params,\n    'decoder_params': decoder_params\n}\n\nvae_state = VAETrainState.create(\n    apply_fn={'encoder': encoder.apply, 'decoder': decoder.apply},\n    params=combined_params,  # Pass combined structure for optimizer initialization\n    tx=vae_tx,\n    encoder_params=encoder_params,\n\
    \    decoder_params=decoder_params\n)\n```\n\n### Additional Fixes\nCopied the training step logic and loss functions from the lineage directory to work with the fixed `VAETrainState` class.\n\n## Result\n- Fixed version: `submission_v4.py`\n- Final score: **0.476**\n- All 50 epochs completed successfully\n- The adversarial VAE training loop now works correctly with proper gradient updates for both encoder and decoder\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v4):**\n```python\nimport os\nos.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'\n\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/Daedalus')\n\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom flax.training import train_state\nimport optax\nfrom tqdm import tqdm\nfrom typing import Any\n\n# Import modular components from storage\nfrom vae_model import\
    \ Encoder, Decoder, reparameterize\nfrom discriminator_model import Discriminator\n\n# Fixed VAETrainState with proper apply_gradients implementation\nclass VAETrainState(train_state.TrainState):\n    \"\"\"A TrainState for the VAE, holding encoder and decoder params.\"\"\"\n    encoder_params: Any\n    decoder_params: Any\n\n    def apply_gradients(self, *, grads, **kwargs):\n        \"\"\"Apply gradients to encoder and decoder params separately.\"\"\"\n        # Create a params structure that matches the grads structure\n        params_tree = {\n            'encoder_params': self.encoder_params,\n            'decoder_params': self.decoder_params\n        }\n\n        updates, new_opt_state = self.tx.update(\n            grads, self.opt_state, params_tree\n        )\n\n        # Apply updates to encoder and decoder params\n        new_encoder_params = optax.apply_updates(self.encoder_params, updates['encoder_params'])\n        new_decoder_params = optax.apply_updates(self.decoder_params,\
    \ updates['decoder_params'])\n\n        return self.replace(\n            step=self.step + 1,\n            encoder_params=new_encoder_params,\n            decoder_params=new_decoder_params,\n            opt_state=new_opt_state,\n            **kwargs,\n        )\n\ndef kl_divergence_loss(mean, log_var):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the KL divergence loss.\"\"\"\n    return -0.5 * jnp.sum(1 + log_var - jnp.square(mean) - jnp.exp(log_var), axis=-1).mean()\n\ndef reconstruction_loss(recon_x, x):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the reconstruction loss (MSE).\"\"\"\n    return jnp.mean((recon_x - x) ** 2)\n\ndef discriminator_loss_fn(disc_logits, batch_labels):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the discriminator's loss (cross-entropy).\"\"\"\n    return optax.softmax_cross_entropy_with_integer_labels(disc_logits, batch_labels).mean()\n\ndef generator_adversarial_loss_fn(disc_logits):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the VAE's adversarial loss.\n    The goal is to make the discriminator's predictions wrong. We achieve this\
    \ by\n    calculating the cross-entropy against a uniform distribution, which encourages\n    the VAE to produce embeddings that make the discriminator uncertain.\n    \"\"\"\n    num_batches = disc_logits.shape[-1]\n    uniform_labels = jnp.ones_like(disc_logits) / num_batches\n    return -jnp.sum(uniform_labels * nn.log_softmax(disc_logits), axis=-1).mean()\n\n@jax.jit\ndef train_step(rng, vae_state, disc_state, batch, batch_labels, kl_weight, adv_weight):\n    \"\"\"Performs a single adversarial training step.\"\"\"\n    rng, vae_rng, disc_rng = jax.random.split(rng, 3)\n\n    def compute_vae_loss(encoder_params, decoder_params):\n        # VAE forward pass\n        mean, log_var = Encoder(hidden_dims=[512, 256], latent_dim=32).apply(\n            {'params': encoder_params}, batch\n        )\n        z = reparameterize(vae_rng, mean, log_var)\n        recon_x = Decoder(hidden_dims=[256, 512], output_dim=batch.shape[-1]).apply(\n            {'params': decoder_params}, z\n        )\n\
    \n        # Discriminator forward pass (for VAE's adversarial loss)\n        # We don't want to train the discriminator here, so we stop gradients\n        disc_logits = disc_state.apply_fn({'params': disc_state.params}, jax.lax.stop_gradient(z))\n\n        # Calculate individual loss components\n        recon_loss_val = reconstruction_loss(recon_x, batch)\n        kl_loss_val = kl_divergence_loss(mean, log_var)\n        adv_loss_val = generator_adversarial_loss_fn(disc_logits)\n\n        total_vae_loss = recon_loss_val + (kl_weight * kl_loss_val) + (adv_weight * adv_loss_val)\n\n        return total_vae_loss, (recon_loss_val, kl_loss_val, adv_loss_val)\n\n    def compute_disc_loss(disc_params):\n        # VAE forward pass to get latent representation (don't train VAE here)\n        mean, log_var = vae_state.apply_fn['encoder']({'params': vae_state.encoder_params}, batch)\n        z = reparameterize(disc_rng, mean, log_var)\n\n        # Discriminator forward pass on the non-gradient\
    \ latent vector\n        disc_logits = disc_state.apply_fn({'params': disc_params}, jax.lax.stop_gradient(z))\n\n        return discriminator_loss_fn(disc_logits, batch_labels)\n\n    # --- VAE Update ---\n    vae_grad_fn = jax.value_and_grad(compute_vae_loss, argnums=(0, 1), has_aux=True)\n    (total_vae_loss, vae_losses), (encoder_grads, decoder_grads) = vae_grad_fn(\n        vae_state.encoder_params, vae_state.decoder_params\n    )\n\n    # Create a combined grads structure for the custom VAETrainState\n    vae_grads = {'encoder_params': encoder_grads, 'decoder_params': decoder_grads}\n    new_vae_state = vae_state.apply_gradients(grads=vae_grads)\n\n    # --- Discriminator Update ---\n    disc_grad_fn = jax.value_and_grad(compute_disc_loss)\n    disc_loss_val, disc_grads = disc_grad_fn(disc_state.params)\n    new_disc_state = disc_state.apply_gradients(grads=disc_grads)\n\n    metrics = {\n        'total_vae_loss': total_vae_loss,\n        'reconstruction_loss': vae_losses[0],\n\
    \        'kl_loss': vae_losses[1],\n        'adversarial_loss': vae_losses[2],\n        'discriminator_loss': disc_loss_val\n    }\n\n    return new_vae_state, new_disc_state, metrics\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Trains an adversarial VAE to learn a batch-invariant embedding.\n    \"\"\"\n    # --- 1. Data Preprocessing ---\n    print(\"Step 1: Preprocessing data...\")\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n    data = adata.X.toarray() if hasattr(adata.X, 'toarray') else adata.X\n    batch_info = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n    batch_labels = batch_info.cat.codes.to_numpy()\n    num_batches = len(batch_info.cat.categories)\n\n    # --- 2. Model and State Initialization ---\n    print(\"Step 2: Initializing models and training states...\")\n    rng = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n    rng, vae_key, disc_key = jax.random.split(rng, 3)\n\n    # Model parameters\n    input_dim = data.shape[1]\n\
    \    latent_dim = 32\n    encoder_dims = [512, 256]\n    decoder_dims = [256, 512]\n    discriminator_dims = [128, 64]\n    learning_rate = 1e-4\n\n    # Init VAE\n    encoder = Encoder(hidden_dims=encoder_dims, latent_dim=latent_dim)\n    decoder = Decoder(hidden_dims=decoder_dims, output_dim=input_dim)\n\n    encoder_params = encoder.init(vae_key, jnp.ones((1, input_dim)))['params']\n    decoder_params = decoder.init(vae_key, jnp.ones((1, latent_dim)))['params']\n\n    # Init Discriminator\n    discriminator = Discriminator(hidden_dims=discriminator_dims, num_batches=num_batches)\n    disc_params = discriminator.init(disc_key, jnp.ones((1, latent_dim)))['params']\n\n    # Create Train States - Fix: use combined params structure\n    vae_tx = optax.adam(learning_rate)\n    disc_tx = optax.adam(learning_rate)\n\n    # Create combined params structure for optimizer state initialization\n    combined_params = {\n        'encoder_params': encoder_params,\n        'decoder_params': decoder_params\n\
    \    }\n\n    vae_state = VAETrainState.create(\n        apply_fn={'encoder': encoder.apply, 'decoder': decoder.apply},\n        params=combined_params,\n        tx=vae_tx,\n        encoder_params=encoder_params,\n        decoder_params=decoder_params\n    )\n\n    disc_state = train_state.TrainState.create(\n        apply_fn=discriminator.apply,\n        params=disc_params,\n        tx=disc_tx\n    )\n\n    # --- 3. Training Loop ---\n    print(\"Step 3: Starting adversarial training loop...\")\n    num_epochs = 50\n    batch_size = 512\n    kl_weight = 0.005\n    adv_weight = 0.5\n\n    num_steps = data.shape[0] // batch_size\n\n    for epoch in range(num_epochs):\n        rng, epoch_rng = jax.random.split(rng)\n        perms = jax.random.permutation(epoch_rng, data.shape[0])\n        data_perm = data[perms, :]\n        labels_perm = batch_labels[perms]\n\n        epoch_metrics = []\n        for i in range(num_steps):\n            batch_idx = i * batch_size\n            batch_data\
    \ = data_perm[batch_idx : batch_idx + batch_size]\n            batch_lbls = labels_perm[batch_idx : batch_idx + batch_size]\n\n            rng, step_rng = jax.random.split(rng)\n            vae_state, disc_state, metrics = train_step(\n                step_rng, vae_state, disc_state, batch_data, batch_lbls, kl_weight, adv_weight\n            )\n            epoch_metrics.append(metrics)\n\n        # Log metrics for the epoch\n        avg_metrics = {k: jnp.mean(jnp.array([m[k] for m in epoch_metrics])) for k in epoch_metrics[0]}\n        print(f\"Epoch {epoch+1}/{num_epochs} - VAE Loss: {avg_metrics['total_vae_loss']:.4f}, Disc Loss: {avg_metrics['discriminator_loss']:.4f}\")\n\n    # --- 4. Generate Final Embedding ---\n    print(\"Step 4: Generating final embedding...\")\n    final_embedding, _ = encoder.apply({'params': vae_state.encoder_params}, data)\n\n    # --- 5. Create Output ---\n    print(\"Step 5: Finalizing output...\")\n    output = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]],\n\
    \        var=adata.var[[]],\n        obsm={'X_emb': jax.device_get(final_embedding)}\n    )\n\n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nStep 1: Preprocessing data...\nStep 2: Initializing models and training states...\nStep 3: Starting adversarial training loop...\nEpoch 1/50 - VAE Loss: 1.8840, Disc Loss: 1.3260\nEpoch 2/50 - VAE Loss: 1.8247, Disc Loss: 1.2232\nEpoch 3/50 - VAE Loss: 1.8121, Disc Loss: 1.1818\nEpoch 4/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7805, Disc Loss: 1.1543\nEpoch 5/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7646, Disc Loss: 1.1340\nEpoch 6/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7541, Disc Loss: 1.1132\nEpoch 7/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7400, Disc Loss: 1.0944\nEpoch 8/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7353, Disc Loss: 1.0859\nEpoch 9/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7332, Disc Loss: 1.0791\nEpoch 10/50 - VAE\
    \ Loss: 1.7346, Disc Loss: 1.0790\nEpoch 11/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7365, Disc Loss: 1.0734\nEpoch 12/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7379, Disc Loss: 1.0723\nEpoch 13/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7379, Disc Loss: 1.0735\nEpoch 14/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7403, Disc Loss: 1.0662\nEpoch 15/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7426, Disc Loss: 1.0643\nEpoch 16/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7446, Disc Loss: 1.0591\nEpoch 17/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7486, Disc Loss: 1.0507\nEpoch 18/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7465, Disc Loss: 1.0442\nEpoch 19/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7415, Disc Loss: 1.0370\nEpoch 20/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7362, Disc Loss: 1.0395\nEpoch 21/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7319, Disc Loss: 1.0338\nEpoch 22/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7304, Disc Loss: 1.0281\nEpoch 23/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7320, Disc Loss: 1.0278\nEpoch 24/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7329, Disc Loss: 1.0231\nEpoch 25/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7346, Disc Loss: 1.0142\nEpoch 26/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7353, Disc Loss: 1.0074\nEpoch 27/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7389, Disc Loss: 1.0007\nEpoch 28/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7416, Disc Loss: 0.9965\nEpoch 29/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7463, Disc Loss: 0.9887\n\
    Epoch 30/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7461, Disc Loss: 0.9878\nEpoch 31/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7451, Disc Loss: 0.9802\nEpoch 32/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7495, Disc Loss: 0.9766\nEpoch 33/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7515, Disc Loss: 0.9679\nEpoch 34/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7535, Disc Loss: 0.9682\nEpoch 35/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7505, Disc Loss: 0.9583\nEpoch 36/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7554, Disc Loss: 0.9543\nEpoch 37/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7624, Disc Loss: 0.9493\nEpoch 38/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7607, Disc Loss: 0.9423\nEpoch 39/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7642, Disc Loss: 0.9454\nEpoch 40/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7609, Disc Loss: 0.9310\nEpoch 41/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7659, Disc Loss: 0.9262\nEpoch 42/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7657, Disc Loss: 0.9164\nEpoch 43/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7687, Disc Loss: 0.9114\nEpoch 44/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7801, Disc Loss: 0.9018\nEpoch 45/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7764, Disc Loss: 0.8935\nEpoch 46/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7855, Disc Loss: 0.8781\nEpoch 47/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7867, Disc Loss: 0.8782\nEpoch 48/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7880, Disc Loss: 0.8649\nEpoch 49/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7970,\
    \ Disc Loss: 0.8556\nEpoch 50/50 - VAE Loss: 1.7992, Disc Loss: 0.8446\nStep 4: Generating final embedding...\nStep 5: Finalizing output...\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: False\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/eb883784-b3e5-4bf1-acf6-682cb5e2c8a1/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: eb883784-b3e5-4bf1-acf6-682cb5e2c8a1\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle\
