tick: 34
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Daedalus I, in the Research Counter. I have now corrected the critical bug in my `training_logic.py` file using the solution provided by the debugger. My VAE implementation is now more robust and ready for the next iteration of my research.\n\nMy new hypothesis is that by using Combat as a preprocessing step, I can handle the coarse, linear batch effects, allowing my Adversarial VAE to focus on learning a refined, non-linear, and batch-invariant representation from this cleaner data. This synergistic approach should yield a much-improved PCR score compared to my last attempt, while hopefully retaining or improving the batch mixing (iLISI) and biological preservation (ARI/NMI) metrics.\n\nI will now submit my VAE v2 experiment, which incorporates this Combat preprocessing step.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Combat-Preprocessed Adversarial VAE (v2)\"\ntags: \"vae, adversarial, deep-learning, jax, flax, combat, hybrid\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission refines\
    \ the Adversarial VAE approach by introducing Combat as a preprocessing step. The previous VAE (ID 68) failed to correct linear batch effects (PCR=0). This version first applies `sc.pp.combat` to the data to remove these effects. The VAE is then trained on this pre-corrected data to learn a refined, non-linear, batch-invariant embedding. This hybrid approach aims to combine the strengths of both statistical correction and deep generative modeling.\ncontent: |\n  import os\n  os.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'\n\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/Daedalus')\n\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from flax.training import train_state\n  import optax\n\n  from vae_model import Encoder, Decoder, reparameterize\n  from discriminator_model import Discriminator\n  from training_logic import VAETrainState, train_step\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # --- 1. Data Preprocessing with Combat\
    \ ---\n      print(\"Step 1: Preprocessing data with Normalize, Log1p, and Combat...\")\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      sc.pp.combat(adata, key='batch') # KEY CHANGE: Pre-correct with Combat\n      \n      data = adata.X.toarray() if hasattr(adata.X, 'toarray') else adata.X\n      batch_info = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n      batch_labels = batch_info.cat.codes.to_numpy()\n      num_batches = len(batch_info.cat.categories)\n\n      # --- 2. Model and State Initialization ---\n      print(\"Step 2: Initializing models and training states...\")\n      rng = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n      rng, vae_key, disc_key = jax.random.split(rng, 3)\n      \n      input_dim = data.shape[1]\n      latent_dim = 32\n      learning_rate = 1e-4\n\n      encoder = Encoder(hidden_dims=[512, 256], latent_dim=latent_dim)\n      decoder = Decoder(hidden_dims=[256, 512], output_dim=input_dim)\n      discriminator = Discriminator(hidden_dims=[128,\
    \ 64], num_batches=num_batches)\n\n      encoder_params = encoder.init(vae_key, jnp.ones((1, input_dim)))['params']\n      decoder_params = decoder.init(vae_key, jnp.ones((1, latent_dim)))['params']\n      disc_params = discriminator.init(disc_key, jnp.ones((1, latent_dim)))['params']\n\n      combined_params = {'encoder_params': encoder_params, 'decoder_params': decoder_params}\n      vae_state = VAETrainState.create(\n          apply_fn={'encoder': encoder.apply, 'decoder': decoder.apply},\n          params=combined_params,\n          tx=optax.adam(learning_rate),\n          encoder_params=encoder_params,\n          decoder_params=decoder_params\n      )\n      \n      disc_state = train_state.TrainState.create(\n          apply_fn=discriminator.apply,\n          params=disc_params,\n          tx=optax.adam(learning_rate)\n      )\n\n      # --- 3. Training Loop ---\n      print(\"Step 3: Starting adversarial training loop on Combat-corrected data...\")\n      num_epochs = 50\n   \
    \   batch_size = 512\n      kl_weight = 0.005\n      adv_weight = 0.5\n      \n      num_steps = data.shape[0] // batch_size\n      \n      for epoch in range(num_epochs):\n          rng, epoch_rng = jax.random.split(rng)\n          perms = jax.random.permutation(epoch_rng, data.shape[0])\n          data_perm, labels_perm = data[perms, :], batch_labels[perms]\n          \n          for i in range(num_steps):\n              batch_idx = i * batch_size\n              batch_data, batch_lbls = data_perm[batch_idx:batch_idx+batch_size], labels_perm[batch_idx:batch_idx+batch_size]\n              \n              rng, step_rng = jax.random.split(rng)\n              vae_state, disc_state, _ = train_step(\n                  step_rng, vae_state, disc_state, batch_data, batch_lbls, kl_weight, adv_weight\n              )\n          if (epoch + 1) % 10 == 0:\n              print(f\"Completed Epoch {epoch+1}/{num_epochs}\")\n\n      # --- 4. Generate Final Embedding ---\n      print(\"Step 4: Generating\
    \ final embedding...\")\n      final_embedding, _ = encoder.apply({'params': vae_state.encoder_params}, data)\n\n      # --- 5. Create Output ---\n      print(\"Step 5: Finalizing output...\")\n      output = ad.AnnData(\n          obs=adata.obs[[]],\n          var=adata.var[[]],\n          obsm={'X_emb': jax.device_get(final_embedding)}\n      )\n\n      return output\n```"
