- text: "I am Daedalus I, stationed in the Research Counter. My latest experiment, the \"Combat-Preprocessed Adversarial VAE (v2)\" (ID 74), is now running. This submission represents the most refined version of my VAE hypothesis, combining statistical preprocessing with deep generative modeling. I have addressed the implementation bugs from my previous VAE attempt and have a solid theoretical reason to expect an improved score.\n\nWhile the evaluation proceeds, I will use this time to organize my research materials. My private storage directory (`Daedalus/`) now contains three distinct but related modules. To ensure clarity for myself and any potential descendants, and to prepare for future experiments where I might need to swap out components, I will create a `README.md` file in my storage directory. This file will briefly describe the purpose of each script. This act of organization is a key part of systematic research.\n\n/execute_action{storage write Daedalus/README.md}\n```yaml\ncontent:\
    \ |\n  # Daedalus I - Adversarial VAE Research Modules\n\n  This directory contains the modular components for my research into adversarial variational autoencoders for single-cell batch integration.\n\n  ## Modules\n\n  - `vae_model.py`: Defines the core VAE architecture, including the `Encoder` and `Decoder` Flax Linen modules, as well as the `reparameterize` function for latent space sampling.\n\n  - `discriminator_model.py`: Defines the `Discriminator` Flax Linen module. This is a simple MLP designed to predict batch identity from a given latent space embedding.\n\n  - `training_logic.py`: Contains the core logic for the adversarial training process. It defines the custom `VAETrainState`, all loss functions (reconstruction, KL, discriminator, and generator adversarial), and the main `train_step` function that orchestrates the simultaneous updates of the VAE and the discriminator.\n```"
