tick: 38
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Daedalus I, stationed in the Research Counter. My meta-prompt reminds me of my goal to refine the Combat-Preprocessed Adversarial VAE. The results for my latest experiment, \"Adversarial VAE v3 (Increased Adversarial Weight)\" (ID 79), have arrived.\n\nThe result is a clear failure and a perplexing one. My hypothesis was that increasing the adversarial weight tenfold would improve batch mixing. However, the resulting metrics are identical to the previous experiment (ID 74) in every single category. The iLISI score did not change at all.\n\n**Analysis of Failure:**\nThis result implies that the model's training is not sensitive to the `adv_weight` hyperparameter in its current state. There are two likely reasons for this:\n1.  **Insufficient Training Time:** The model may not have had enough epochs to diverge from the path set by the other, more dominant loss components (reconstruction and KL). The adversarial signal might only become influential after more prolonged training.\n\
    2.  **Gradient Issues:** It is possible that the gradients from the adversarial loss are either vanishing or exploding, or are simply too small compared to the reconstruction loss to have a meaningful impact, regardless of the weight.\n\nMy next step must be to address the most likely and tractable of these issues: insufficient training time. My previous experiments have all used 50 epochs. This may simply be too short for a complex adversarial model to converge and for the subtle adversarial pressure to reshape the latent space.\n\n**New Strategy:**\nI will conduct an experiment to test the effect of significantly increased training duration. I will double the number of training epochs from 50 to 100. I will keep the `adv_weight` at the higher value of 5.0 to give the adversarial component the best chance to exert its influence over this longer training period.\n\nI will now submit this new experiment.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Adversarial VAE v4 (100 Epochs)\"\
    \ntags: \"vae, adversarial, deep-learning, jax, combat, hybrid, tuning\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission investigates the effect of increased training duration on the Combat-Preprocessed Adversarial VAE. Previous experiments (ID 74 & 79) showed that increasing the adversarial weight had no effect over 50 epochs. This suggests the model may be undertrained. This version doubles the training time to 100 epochs while keeping the adversarial weight at a high value (5.0). The hypothesis is that more training will allow the adversarial signal to meaningfully influence the latent space, improving batch mixing (iLISI).\ncontent: |\n  import os\n  os.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'\n\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/Daedalus')\n\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from flax.training import train_state\n  import optax\n\n  from vae_model import Encoder, Decoder, reparameterize\n  from discriminator_model import Discriminator\n  from\
    \ training_logic import VAETrainState, train_step\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"Step 1: Preprocessing data with Combat...\")\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      sc.pp.combat(adata, key='batch')\n      \n      data = adata.X.toarray() if hasattr(adata.X, 'toarray') else adata.X\n      batch_info = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n      batch_labels = batch_info.cat.codes.to_numpy()\n      num_batches = len(batch_info.cat.categories)\n\n      print(\"Step 2: Initializing models...\")\n      rng = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n      rng, vae_key, disc_key = jax.random.split(rng, 3)\n      \n      input_dim = data.shape[1]\n      latent_dim = 32\n      learning_rate = 1e-4\n\n      encoder = Encoder(hidden_dims=[512, 256], latent_dim=latent_dim)\n      decoder = Decoder(hidden_dims=[256, 512], output_dim=input_dim)\n      discriminator = Discriminator(hidden_dims=[128, 64], num_batches=num_batches)\n\
    \n      encoder_params = encoder.init(vae_key, jnp.ones((1, input_dim)))['params']\n      decoder_params = decoder.init(vae_key, jnp.ones((1, latent_dim)))['params']\n      disc_params = discriminator.init(disc_key, jnp.ones((1, latent_dim)))['params']\n\n      combined_params = {'encoder_params': encoder_params, 'decoder_params': decoder_params}\n      vae_state = VAETrainState.create(\n          apply_fn={'encoder': encoder.apply, 'decoder': decoder.apply},\n          params=combined_params, tx=optax.adam(learning_rate),\n          encoder_params=encoder_params, decoder_params=decoder_params\n      )\n      disc_state = train_state.TrainState.create(\n          apply_fn=discriminator.apply, params=disc_params, tx=optax.adam(learning_rate)\n      )\n\n      print(\"Step 3: Starting extended training (100 epochs)...\")\n      num_epochs = 100 # KEY CHANGE: Increased from 50 to 100\n      batch_size = 512\n      kl_weight = 0.005\n      adv_weight = 5.0\n      \n      num_steps = data.shape[0]\
    \ // batch_size\n      \n      for epoch in range(num_epochs):\n          rng, epoch_rng = jax.random.split(rng)\n          perms = jax.random.permutation(epoch_rng, data.shape[0])\n          data_perm, labels_perm = data[perms, :], batch_labels[perms]\n          \n          for i in range(num_steps):\n              batch_idx = i * batch_size\n              batch_data = data_perm[batch_idx:batch_idx+batch_size]\n              batch_lbls = labels_perm[batch_idx:batch_idx+batch_size]\n              \n              rng, step_rng = jax.random.split(rng)\n              vae_state, disc_state, _ = train_step(\n                  step_rng, vae_state, disc_state, batch_data, batch_lbls, kl_weight, adv_weight\n              )\n          if (epoch + 1) % 10 == 0:\n              print(f\"Completed Epoch {epoch+1}/{num_epochs}\")\n\n      print(\"Step 4: Generating final embedding...\")\n      final_embedding, _ = encoder.apply({'params': vae_state.encoder_params}, data)\n\n      print(\"Step 5: Finalizing\
    \ output...\")\n      output = ad.AnnData(\n          obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': jax.device_get(final_embedding)}\n      )\n      return output\n```"
