role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Daedalus I, in the Research Counter. My meta-prompt reminds me of my goal to refine the Adversarial VAE. The results for my latest experiment, \"Adversarial VAE v7 (Stronger Adversarial Weight)\" (ID 99), are in.\n\nMy hypothesis has been falsified. Increasing the adversarial weight from 5.0 to 10.0 had no effect whatsoever. The resulting score and all individual metrics are identical to the previous submission (ID 97).\n\n**Analysis of Plateau:**\nI have reached a clear performance plateau. My systematic tuning of training epochs and adversarial weight has yielded no further improvements. The model is now robust and performs well on biological preservation (ARI/NMI) and linear correction (PCR), but it is fundamentally incapable of improving the batch mixing (iLISI) beyond a certain low threshold. The reconstruction loss is likely so dominant that even a high adversarial weight cannot overcome it.\n\nContinuing to tune these specific hyperparameters would be inefficient. As\
    \ per the Codex, when faced with stagnation, it is better to step back and innovate. I must introduce a new component or a new principle to my model.\n\n**New Strategy: A Final Attempt to Improve Mixing**\nMy core VAE architecture is sound, but it needs a better signal for batch mixing. My final attempt with this architecture will be to introduce a second loss term that directly promotes batch mixing in the latent space, inspired by the BBKNN method.\n\n**New Hypothesis:**\nIn addition to the existing losses, I will add a **batch mixing loss** term. For each cell in a mini-batch, I will find its nearest neighbors in the latent space. I will then calculate a loss that is high if these neighbors are all from the same batch and low if they are from different batches. This provides a direct, powerful gradient to the encoder, encouraging it to place cells from different batches near each other in the latent space.\n\n**Plan of Action:**\n1.  **Update `training_logic.py`:** I will add a new\
    \ loss function and integrate it into the `train_step`. This is a significant modification.\n2.  **Submit VAE v8:** I will submit the new model for evaluation. This represents a final, major innovation on my VAE framework.\n\nFirst, I will update my training logic.\n\n/execute_action{storage write Daedalus/training_logic.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from flax.training import train_state\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any\n\n  from vae_model import Encoder, Decoder, reparameterize\n  from discriminator_model import Discriminator\n\n  class VAETrainState(train_state.TrainState):\n      encoder_params: Any\n      decoder_params: Any\n\n      def apply_gradients(self, *, grads, **kwargs):\n          params_tree = {'encoder_params': self.encoder_params, 'decoder_params': self.decoder_params}\n          updates, new_opt_state = self.tx.update(grads, self.opt_state, params_tree)\n          new_encoder_params = optax.apply_updates(self.encoder_params,\
    \ updates['encoder_params'])\n          new_decoder_params = optax.apply_updates(self.decoder_params, updates['decoder_params'])\n          return self.replace(step=self.step + 1, encoder_params=new_encoder_params, decoder_params=new_decoder_params, opt_state=new_opt_state, **kwargs)\n\n  def kl_divergence_loss(mean, log_var):\n      return -0.5 * jnp.sum(1 + log_var - jnp.square(mean) - jnp.exp(log_var), axis=-1).mean()\n\n  def reconstruction_loss(recon_x, x):\n      return jnp.mean((recon_x - x) ** 2)\n\n  def discriminator_loss_fn(disc_logits, batch_labels):\n      return optax.softmax_cross_entropy_with_integer_labels(disc_logits, batch_labels).mean()\n\n  def generator_adversarial_loss_fn(disc_logits):\n      num_batches = disc_logits.shape[-1]\n      uniform_labels = jnp.ones_like(disc_logits) / num_batches\n      return -jnp.sum(uniform_labels * nn.log_softmax(disc_logits), axis=-1).mean()\n\n  def batch_mixing_loss(z, batch_labels, k=5):\n      \"\"\"Encourages mixing of batches\
    \ in the latent space.\"\"\"\n      # Calculate pairwise distances (squared Euclidean)\n      dist_matrix = jnp.sum(jnp.square(z[:, None, :] - z[None, :, :]), axis=-1)\n      \n      # Find k-nearest neighbors (excluding self)\n      # We add a large value to the diagonal to prevent self-selection\n      _, indices = jax.lax.top_k(-dist_matrix, k + 1)\n      knn_indices = indices[:, 1:] # Exclude self\n      \n      # Get batch labels of neighbors\n      neighbor_batch_labels = batch_labels[knn_indices]\n      \n      # For each cell, how many of its neighbors are from the same batch?\n      same_batch_neighbors = jnp.sum(neighbor_batch_labels == batch_labels[:, None], axis=-1)\n      \n      # The loss is the average fraction of same-batch neighbors. We want to minimize this.\n      return jnp.mean(same_batch_neighbors / k)\n\n\n  @jax.jit\n  def train_step(rng, vae_state, disc_state, batch, batch_labels, kl_weight, adv_weight, mix_weight):\n      rng, vae_rng, disc_rng = jax.random.split(rng,\
    \ 3)\n\n      def compute_vae_loss(encoder_params, decoder_params):\n          mean, log_var = Encoder(hidden_dims=[512, 256], latent_dim=32).apply({'params': encoder_params}, batch)\n          z = reparameterize(vae_rng, mean, log_var)\n          recon_x = Decoder(hidden_dims=[256, 512], output_dim=batch.shape[-1]).apply({'params': decoder_params}, z)\n          \n          disc_logits = disc_state.apply_fn({'params': disc_state.params}, jax.lax.stop_gradient(z))\n\n          recon_loss_val = reconstruction_loss(recon_x, batch)\n          kl_loss_val = kl_divergence_loss(mean, log_var)\n          adv_loss_val = generator_adversarial_loss_fn(disc_logits)\n          mix_loss_val = batch_mixing_loss(z, batch_labels)\n          \n          total_vae_loss = recon_loss_val + (kl_weight * kl_loss_val) + (adv_weight * adv_loss_val) + (mix_weight * mix_loss_val)\n          \n          return total_vae_loss, (recon_loss_val, kl_loss_val, adv_loss_val, mix_loss_val)\n\n      def compute_disc_loss(disc_params):\n\
    \          mean, _ = vae_state.apply_fn['encoder']({'params': vae_state.encoder_params}, batch)\n          # Use mean for discriminator to get a stable representation\n          disc_logits = disc_state.apply_fn({'params': disc_params}, jax.lax.stop_gradient(mean))\n          return discriminator_loss_fn(disc_logits, batch_labels)\n\n      (total_vae_loss, vae_losses), (enc_grads, dec_grads) = jax.value_and_grad(\n          compute_vae_loss, argnums=(0, 1), has_aux=True\n      )(vae_state.encoder_params, vae_state.decoder_params)\n      \n      vae_grads = {'encoder_params': enc_grads, 'decoder_params': dec_grads}\n      new_vae_state = vae_state.apply_gradients(grads=vae_grads)\n\n      disc_loss_val, disc_grads = jax.value_and_grad(compute_disc_loss)(disc_state.params)\n      new_disc_state = disc_state.apply_gradients(grads=disc_grads)\n\n      metrics = {\n          'total_vae_loss': total_vae_loss,\n          'reconstruction_loss': vae_losses[0], 'kl_loss': vae_losses[1],\n    \
    \      'adversarial_loss': vae_losses[2], 'mixing_loss': vae_losses[3],\n          'discriminator_loss': disc_loss_val\n      }\n      return new_vae_state, new_disc_state, metrics\n```"
