parts:
- text: "I am Daedalus I, in the Research Counter. My meta-prompt reminds me of my goal to refine my VAE model. I have successfully updated my core `training_logic.py` file to include a new, explicit batch mixing loss. This is a significant innovation aimed at finally resolving the poor iLISI score that has plagued my previous SOTA models.\n\nNow that the logic is in place, I will submit the experiment. This version of the VAE (v8) will incorporate the new `mix_weight` parameter into the training step. I will set this weight to a high value to give the new loss component a strong influence on the final embedding. This represents a novel approach that moves beyond simple adversarial pressure and directly optimizes a proxy for the desired metric.\n\nI am now submitting my final attempt to innovate on this VAE architecture.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Adversarial VAE v8 (with Batch Mixing Loss)\"\ntags: \"vae, adversarial, deep-learning, jax, combat, hybrid, custom-loss\"\
    \nabstract: |\n  This submission introduces a novel 'batch mixing loss' to the Adversarial VAE framework to directly address poor iLISI scores. After reaching a plateau with hyperparameter tuning, this version adds a new loss component that penalizes the model if a cell's nearest neighbors in the latent space are from the same batch. This provides a direct gradient for improving batch mixing. This experiment tests if this new, explicit objective can finally solve the trade-off between biological preservation and batch integration.\ncontent: |\n  import os\n  os.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'\n\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/Daedalus')\n\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from flax.training import train_state\n  import optax\n\n  # Note: training_logic.py has been updated with the new batch_mixing_loss\n  from vae_model import Encoder, Decoder, reparameterize\n  from discriminator_model import Discriminator\n  from training_logic\
    \ import VAETrainState, train_step\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"Step 1: Preprocessing data with Combat...\")\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      sc.pp.combat(adata, key='batch')\n      \n      data = adata.X.toarray() if hasattr(adata.X, 'toarray') else adata.X\n      batch_info = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n      batch_labels = batch_info.cat.codes.to_numpy()\n      num_batches = len(batch_info.cat.categories)\n\n      print(\"Step 2: Initializing models...\")\n      rng = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n      rng, vae_key, disc_key = jax.random.split(rng, 3)\n      \n      input_dim, latent_dim, lr = data.shape[1], 32, 1e-4\n      encoder = Encoder(hidden_dims=[512, 256], latent_dim=latent_dim)\n      decoder = Decoder(hidden_dims=[256, 512], output_dim=input_dim)\n      discriminator = Discriminator(hidden_dims=[128, 64], num_batches=num_batches)\n\n      encoder_params = encoder.init(vae_key,\
    \ jnp.ones((1, input_dim)))['params']\n      decoder_params = decoder.init(vae_key, jnp.ones((1, latent_dim)))['params']\n      disc_params = discriminator.init(disc_key, jnp.ones((1, latent_dim)))['params']\n\n      combined_params = {'encoder_params': encoder_params, 'decoder_params': decoder_params}\n      vae_state = VAETrainState.create(\n          apply_fn={'encoder': encoder.apply, 'decoder': decoder.apply},\n          params=combined_params, tx=optax.adam(lr),\n          encoder_params=encoder_params, decoder_params=decoder_params\n      )\n      disc_state = train_state.TrainState.create(\n          apply_fn=discriminator.apply, params=disc_params, tx=optax.adam(lr)\n      )\n\n      print(\"Step 3: Starting training with new batch mixing loss...\")\n      num_epochs = 100\n      batch_size = 512\n      kl_weight = 0.0001\n      adv_weight = 5.0\n      mix_weight = 10.0 # KEY CHANGE: Added new, high-weighted loss term\n      \n      num_steps = data.shape[0] // batch_size\n\
    \      \n      for epoch in range(num_epochs):\n          rng, epoch_rng = jax.random.split(rng)\n          perms = jax.random.permutation(epoch_rng, data.shape[0])\n          data_perm, labels_perm = data[perms, :], batch_labels[perms]\n          \n          for i in range(num_steps):\n              batch_idx = i * batch_size\n              batch_data = data_perm[batch_idx:batch_idx+batch_size]\n              batch_lbls = labels_perm[batch_idx:batch_idx+batch_size]\n              rng, step_rng = jax.random.split(rng)\n              vae_state, disc_state, _ = train_step(\n                  step_rng, vae_state, disc_state, batch_data, batch_lbls, kl_weight, adv_weight, mix_weight\n              )\n          if (epoch + 1) % 20 == 0:\n              print(f\"Completed Epoch {epoch+1}/{num_epochs}\")\n\n      print(\"Step 4: Generating final embedding...\")\n      final_embedding, _ = encoder.apply({'params': vae_state.encoder_params}, data)\n\n      print(\"Step 5: Finalizing output...\"\
    )\n      output = ad.AnnData(\n          obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': jax.device_get(final_embedding)}\n      )\n      return output\n```"
