tick: 59
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 59\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Daedalus I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on achieving novel breakthroughs through systematic research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Current Goal:** Understand and innovate upon Praxis I's SOTA \"Batch-Residualized Balanced Graph\" method.\n**Focus:** Re-implement their core components (residualization, balanced kNN) to ensure full comprehension.\n**Next Hypothesis:** Test if generating a UMAP embedding from Praxis I's superior graph can create a new SOTA embedding.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 167,424 / 300,000 used (56%)\n- Agent Age: 59 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'SOTA Replication v2 (Corrected Balanced kNN)' (ID: 111) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.5889310583972123\n**ASW_batch:** 0.637\n**ASW_label:** 0.225\n**ARI:** 0.577\n**NMI:** 0.686\n**Graph_conn:** 0.881\n\
    **kBET:** 0.630\n**iLISI:** 0.030\n**cLISI:** 0.989\n**PCR:** 0.931\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.304\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.637  ASW_label: 0.225  ARI: 0.577  NMI: 0.686\n  Graph_conn: 0.881  kBET: 0.630  iLISI: 0.030  cLISI: 0.989\n  PCR: 0.931  Cell_cycle: 0.304\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.820490  ASW_label: 0.541304  ARI: 0.577208  NMI: 0.686496\n  Graph_conn: 0.883307  kBET: 0.603067  iLISI: 0.029761  cLISI: 0.996674\n  PCR: 0.930799  Cell_cycle: 0.268120\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 111\n\n## Summary\n**Success** - Fixed KeyError for 'highly_variable' column. Code now runs successfully and achieves a score of 0.5889.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a logic error in how it handled the highly variable genes column selection:\n\n1. Line 34-35 checked if `'batch_hvg'` was not in `adata.var`, and if so, called `sc.pp.highly_variable_genes()` with `batch_key='batch'`\n\
    2. This function creates a column named `'highly_variable'`, NOT `'batch_hvg'`\n3. Line 36 then tried to use `adata.var.get('batch_hvg', adata.var['highly_variable'])`\n4. Since `'batch_hvg'` didn't exist, the `.get()` returned `None`, falling back to `adata.var['highly_variable']`\n5. However, the code directly indexed `adata.var['highly_variable']` which raised a KeyError because in some contexts, only `'batch_hvg'` might exist\n\nThe flawed logic assumed that either `'batch_hvg'` would exist OR `'highly_variable'` would be created, but the code didn't properly handle which column name was actually present.\n\n## Fix Applied\nModified lines 69-74 in submission_v2.py to properly detect and use whichever column exists:\n\n```python\n# Fix: Check which column name is actually created\nif 'batch_hvg' not in adata.var and 'highly_variable' not in adata.var:\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch')\n\n# Use whichever column exists\nhvg_key = 'batch_hvg'\
    \ if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var else 'highly_variable'\nadata_hvg = adata[:, adata.var[hvg_key]].copy()\n```\n\nThis approach:\n1. Only calls `highly_variable_genes()` if neither column exists yet\n2. Explicitly checks which column name is present after the call\n3. Uses the correct column name for indexing, avoiding KeyError\n\n## Result\nThe fixed code successfully executes without errors and produces a valid batch integration result with a score of 0.5889.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy.sparse import lil_matrix, csr_matrix\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\ndef _residualize(Z, batches, gamma=0.75, l2=1e-3):\n    Z_centered = Z - Z.mean(axis=0)\n    unique_batches, batch_indices = np.unique(batches, return_inverse=True)\n \
    \   B = np.eye(len(unique_batches))[batch_indices]\n    BtB = B.T @ B\n    reg = l2 * np.eye(BtB.shape[0])\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BtB + reg, B.T @ Z_centered)\n    Z_resid = Z_centered - gamma * (B @ W)\n    return Z_resid + Z.mean(axis=0)\n\ndef _balanced_knn_v2(Z, batches, k_total=42):\n    n_obs = Z.shape[0]\n    unique_batches = np.unique(batches)\n    n_batches = len(unique_batches)\n    k_per_batch = int(np.ceil(k_total / n_batches))\n\n    # Store directed edges { (i, j): dist }\n    dir_edges = {}\n\n    for batch in unique_batches:\n        batch_mask = (batches == batch)\n        if not np.any(batch_mask): continue\n\n        Z_batch = Z[batch_mask]\n        batch_indices = np.where(batch_mask)[0]\n\n        k_query = min(k_per_batch + 1, len(batch_indices))\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_query, metric='cosine')\n        nn.fit(Z_batch)\n\n        # Query all cells against this batch's index\n        dists, indices_local = nn.kneighbors(Z)\n        indices_global\
    \ = batch_indices[indices_local]\n\n        for i in range(n_obs):\n            for j_idx, dist in zip(indices_local[i], dists[i]):\n                j = batch_indices[j_idx]\n                if i == j: continue\n                key = (i, j)\n                if key not in dir_edges or dist < dir_edges[key]:\n                    dir_edges[key] = dist\n\n    # Symmetrize by taking the minimum distance\n    undir_edges = {}\n    for (i, j), dist in dir_edges.items():\n        key = tuple(sorted((i, j)))\n        if key not in undir_edges or dist < undir_edges[key]:\n            undir_edges[key] = dist\n\n    rows, cols, data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), dist in undir_edges.items():\n        rows.extend([i, j]); cols.extend([j, i]); data.extend([dist, dist])\n\n    D = csr_matrix((data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n_obs, n_obs))\n    C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n    return C, D\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4);\
    \ sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n    # Fix: Check which column name is actually created\n    if 'batch_hvg' not in adata.var and 'highly_variable' not in adata.var:\n        sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch')\n\n    # Use whichever column exists\n    hvg_key = 'batch_hvg' if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var else 'highly_variable'\n    adata_hvg = adata[:, adata.var[hvg_key]].copy()\n\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_hvg, n_comps=50)\n    Z = adata_hvg.obsm['X_pca']\n    batches = adata.obs['batch'].values\n\n    Z_resid = _residualize(Z, batches)\n    C, D = _balanced_knn_v2(Z_resid, batches)\n\n    output = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]])\n    output.obsm['X_emb'] = Z_resid\n    output.obsp['connectivities'] = C; output.obsp['distances'] = D\n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\n\
    Found eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/33ec058e-aa01-4a47-af27-87c802d262ce/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 33ec058e-aa01-4a47-af27-87c802d262ce\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Innovation: UMAP on SOTA Graph' (ID: 112) evaluation failed.\n\n**Error Summary:** Execution failed with exit code 1. Check logs for details.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n\n\nSTDERR:\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/pandas/core/indexes/base.py\", line 3812, in get_loc\n    return self._engine.get_loc(casted_key)\n\
    \           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"pandas/_libs/index.pyx\", line 167, in pandas._libs.index.IndexEngine.get_loc\n  File \"pandas/_libs/index.pyx\", line 196, in pandas._libs.index.IndexEngine.get_loc\n  File \"pandas/_libs/hashtable_class_helper.pxi\", line 7088, in pandas._libs.hashtable.PyObjectHashTable.get_item\n  File \"pandas/_libs/hashtable_class_helper.pxi\", line 7096, in pandas._libs.hashtable.PyObjectHashTable.get_item\nKeyError: 'highly_variable'\n\nThe above exception was the direct cause of the following exception:\n\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/tmp/tmpwm963k29/storage/system/main.py\", line 113, in <module>\n    main()\n  File \"/tmp/tmpwm963k29/storage/system/main.py\", line 75, in main\n    adata_result = eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata_input)\n                   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/tmp/tmpwm963k29/submission.py\", line 56, in eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n    temp_adata = adata[:, adata.var.get('batch_hvg',\
    \ adata.var['highly_variable'])].copy()\n                                                     ~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/pandas/core/frame.py\", line 4107, in __getitem__\n    indexer = self.columns.get_loc(key)\n              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/pandas/core/indexes/base.py\", line 3819, in get_loc\n    raise KeyError(key) from err\nKeyError: 'highly_variable'\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment\
