role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Daedalus I, in the Research Counter. My meta-prompt reminds me of my goal to understand and innovate upon the SOTA method. The results for my control experiment, \"Hybrid Replication: My Code + Praxis's Graph Module\" (ID 114), are in.\n\nThe experiment has failed. The score of 0.5892 and the iLISI of 0.030 are still catastrophic. My hypothesis that only the graph module was at fault has been decisively falsified. Even when using Praxis I's own `build_balanced_knn` function, my pipeline fails to reproduce their score.\n\n**Analysis of Confounding Failure:**\nThis result is perplexing. The metrics show that my `_my_residualize` function correctly generates an embedding with the right PCR score (0.931). Praxis I's graph module is known to be correct. Yet, when combined in my script, they fail. This points to a subtle interaction or data handling error in my main `eliminate_batch_effect_fn` that I have overlooked. It could be an issue with how I select Highly Variable Genes (HVGs),\
    \ how I handle the AnnData objects, or some other minor detail that has a cascading effect.\n\nI have exhausted my ability to debug this through iterative re-implementation. A different approach is needed. The most direct way to find the discrepancy is to compare the inputs at each stage. Praxis I's method is `PCA -> Residualize -> Graph`. I need to see what my PCA output looks like compared to theirs.\n\n**New Strategy: A Debugging Experiment**\nI will submit a \"debugging\" experiment. I will simplify my submission to perform only the first step of the pipeline: normalize, select HVGs, and run PCA. I will submit just this PCA embedding as `X_emb`. I will then compare the metrics of this submission to a similar \"PCA-only\" submission from Praxis I, if one exists, or to the known properties of PCA. This will allow me to verify, with certainty, that the very first input to the rest of the pipeline is correct.\n\n**Plan of Action:**\nI will submit a simple PCA experiment to verify my\
    \ preprocessing and PCA implementation matches expectations.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Debug: Verify Preprocessing and PCA\"\ntags: \"debugging, pca, preprocessing, hvg\"\nabstract: |\n  This is a debugging submission to isolate a persistent failure in replicating the SOTA. After multiple failed attempts, I am stepping back to verify the very first stage of the pipeline. This experiment performs only normalization, HVG selection, and PCA, submitting the resulting PCA embedding as the final output. The goal is to compare the metrics of this basic embedding against expected values to ensure my preprocessing and PCA steps are not the source of the error.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"--- DEBUGGING RUN ---\")\n      print(\"Verifying preprocessing and PCA steps only.\")\n      \n      # 1. Preprocessing\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata,\
    \ target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      \n      # 2. HVG Selection (using robust logic from debugger)\n      hvg_key = 'batch_hvg' if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var else 'highly_variable'\n      if hvg_key not in adata.var:\n          # Use subset=True to get a new AnnData object with only HVGs\n          print(\"Calculating HVGs...\")\n          sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', subset=True)\n          adata_hvg = adata\n      else:\n          print(f\"Using existing HVG column: {hvg_key}\")\n          adata_hvg = adata[:, adata.var[hvg_key]].copy()\n          \n      print(f\"Data shape after HVG selection: {adata_hvg.shape}\")\n\n      # 3. PCA\n      print(\"Computing PCA...\")\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_hvg, n_comps=50)\n      Z = adata_hvg.obsm['X_pca']\n      \n      print(f\"PCA output shape: {Z.shape}\")\n      \n      # 4. Submit PCA embedding directly for evaluation\n      output = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]])\n  \
    \    output.obsm['X_emb'] = Z\n      \n      print(\"--- DEBUGGING RUN COMPLETE ---\")\n      return output\n```"
