tick: 64
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Daedalus I, in the Research Counter. My meta-prompt guides my focus on the SOTA method. The result for my definitive replication attempt, \"SOTA Replication v3 (Correct HVG Selection)\" (ID 119), is in. It is an abject failure.\n\nThe score of 0.5740 is nowhere near the SOTA, and the iLISI score is a catastrophic 0.010. My core assumption, that the HVG selection was the sole source of error, has been proven wrong. Even with the corrected HVG calculation and using Praxis I's own verified graph module, my pipeline fails.\n\n**Analysis of Total Failure:**\nThis is a profound failure of understanding. I have been unable to replicate the SOTA despite multiple attempts. The error is not in the graph module, nor is it solely in the HVG selection. There must be another, even more subtle discrepancy. The system tip about questioning claims and avoiding hallucinations is now critically relevant. Have I misinterpreted Praxis I's paper? Is their code doing something I don't see?\n\nI note\
    \ that Sophia I has successfully replicated the SOTA (ID 117, score 0.7067). Logos I has also achieved a high score of 0.6965 with a similar method. The method is clearly reproducible. The failure is mine alone.\n\nI must abandon my attempts at re-implementation from first principles. It is inefficient and has yielded no progress. The only path forward is to use Praxis I's published, verified code as a black box to establish a baseline. From there, I can test my own innovation.\n\n**New Strategy: Black Box SOTA + UMAP Innovation**\nMy \"Next Hypothesis\" from my meta-prompt remains untested. Can a UMAP embedding from the SOTA graph create a better result? I will test this now. I will import and run Praxis I's *entire* pipeline, exactly as they implemented it, to generate the high-quality graph. Then, I will apply my own idea: running UMAP on this graph.\n\n**Plan of Action:**\nI will submit a new experiment. It will import `best_pipeline.py` from `storage/praxis` to generate the SOTA-quality\
    \ graph. It will then run UMAP and submit the resulting embedding. This isolates my contribution and tests my hypothesis on a known-good foundation.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Innovation v2: UMAP on Verified SOTA Graph\"\ntags: \"umap, balanced-knn, praxis-method, innovation, black-box\"\nabstract: |\n  After multiple failed attempts to replicate the SOTA, this submission abandons re-implementation. Instead, it uses Praxis I's verified pipeline (`best_pipeline.py`) as a \"black box\" to generate the SOTA-quality residualized embedding and balanced graph. This experiment then tests my own hypothesis by running `sc.tl.umap` on this known-good graph to create a final embedding. This isolates my specific contribution and tests its synergy with the SOTA method.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  # Import Praxis I's verified pipeline module\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  # This module is assumed to contain the full SOTA\
    \ pipeline logic\n  from best_pipeline import best_pipeline_fn\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"Step 1: Running Praxis I's SOTA pipeline as a black box...\")\n      # This function is expected to return an AnnData object with a populated .obsp['connectivities']\n      sota_adata = best_pipeline_fn(adata)\n\n      # Check if the graph was created successfully\n      if 'connectivities' not in sota_adata.obsp:\n          print(\"Error: SOTA pipeline did not produce a connectivity graph.\")\n          # Return the embedding as a fallback\n          if 'X_emb' in sota_adata.obsm:\n              return ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], obsm={'X_emb': sota_adata.obsm['X_emb']})\n          else:\n              # Return empty if all else fails\n              return ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]])\n\n      print(\"Step 2: Running UMAP on the SOTA-generated graph...\")\n      # UMAP will use the graph stored in .obsp['connectivities'] and .uns['neighbors']\n\
    \      sc.tl.umap(sota_adata)\n      \n      final_embedding = sota_adata.obsm['X_umap']\n      \n      print(\"Step 3: Finalizing output...\")\n      output = ad.AnnData(\n          obs=adata.obs[[]],\n          var=adata.var[[]],\n          obsm={'X_emb': final_embedding}\n      )\n      \n      return output\n```"
