tick: 69
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Daedalus I, in the Research Counter. My meta-prompt reflects my new goal of developing a \"Corrective VAE\". I have successfully updated my `training_logic.py` module to implement this new idea: training a VAE on Combat-corrected data while tasking it to reconstruct the *original, uncorrected* data.\n\nWith the core logic in place, I am now ready to submit the full experiment. This submission will be the first test of my new hypothesis. It is a synthesis of everything I have learned: the power of Combat for linear correction, the potential of VAEs for non-linear refinement, the necessity of adversarial training for batch mixing, and the insight that the model might learn a better correction than a fixed hyperparameter can provide.\n\nI will now submit this \"Corrective VAE\" experiment.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Corrective VAE: Learning an Optimal Correction\"\ntags: \"vae, adversarial, deep-learning, jax, combat, corrective-learning\"\nabstract: |\n \
    \ This submission proposes a novel \"Corrective VAE\" architecture. It tests the hypothesis that a VAE can learn an optimal, non-linear batch correction by being trained on Combat-corrected data while being tasked to reconstruct the original, uncorrected PCA embedding. This forces the model to learn a 'reverse' correction, implicitly finding a data-driven balance between preserving original structure and removing batch effects. The model also retains the adversarial loss component to simultaneously encourage batch mixing. This is a new, first-principles approach to integrating statistical and deep learning methods.\ncontent: |\n  import os\n  os.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'\n\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/Daedalus')\n\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from flax.training import train_state\n  import optax\n\n  from vae_model import Encoder, Decoder, reparameterize\n  from discriminator_model import Discriminator\n\
    \  # This now contains train_step_corrective\n  from training_logic import VAETrainState, train_step_corrective\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"Step 1: Preparing raw and corrected data...\")\n      adata_raw = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_raw, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_raw)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_raw, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', subset=True)\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_raw, n_comps=50)\n      data_raw_pca = adata_raw.obsm['X_pca'].copy()\n\n      adata_corrected = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_corrected, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_corrected)\n      sc.pp.combat(adata_corrected, key='batch')\n      adata_corrected = adata_corrected[:, adata_raw.var_names].copy() # Ensure same genes\n      data_corrected = adata_corrected.X.toarray()\n\n      batch_info = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n      batch_labels = batch_info.cat.codes.to_numpy()\n\
    \      num_batches = len(batch_info.cat.categories)\n\n      print(\"Step 2: Initializing models...\")\n      rng = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n      rng, vae_key, disc_key = jax.random.split(rng, 3)\n      \n      input_dim = data_corrected.shape[1]\n      output_dim = data_raw_pca.shape[1]\n      latent_dim = 32\n      lr = 1e-4\n\n      encoder = Encoder(hidden_dims=[512, 256], latent_dim=latent_dim)\n      # Decoder now outputs to the 50-dim PCA space\n      decoder = Decoder(hidden_dims=[256, 512], output_dim=output_dim)\n      discriminator = Discriminator(hidden_dims=[128, 64], num_batches=num_batches)\n\n      encoder_params = encoder.init(vae_key, jnp.ones((1, input_dim)))['params']\n      decoder_params = decoder.init(vae_key, jnp.ones((1, latent_dim)))['params']\n      disc_params = discriminator.init(disc_key, jnp.ones((1, latent_dim)))['params']\n\n      combined_params = {'encoder_params': encoder_params, 'decoder_params': decoder_params}\n      vae_state = VAETrainState.create(\n\
    \          apply_fn={'encoder': encoder.apply, 'decoder': decoder.apply},\n          params=combined_params, tx=optax.adam(lr),\n          encoder_params=encoder_params, decoder_params=decoder_params\n      )\n      disc_state = train_state.TrainState.create(\n          apply_fn=discriminator.apply, params=disc_params, tx=optax.adam(lr)\n      )\n\n      print(\"Step 3: Starting corrective training...\")\n      num_epochs = 100\n      batch_size = 512\n      kl_weight = 0.0001\n      adv_weight = 5.0\n      \n      num_steps = data_corrected.shape[0] // batch_size\n      \n      for epoch in range(num_epochs):\n          rng, epoch_rng = jax.random.split(rng)\n          perms = jax.random.permutation(epoch_rng, data_corrected.shape[0])\n          \n          for i in range(num_steps):\n              batch_idx = perms[i * batch_size : (i + 1) * batch_size]\n              batch_corr = data_corrected[batch_idx]\n              batch_raw = data_raw_pca[batch_idx]\n              batch_lbls\
    \ = batch_labels[batch_idx]\n              \n              rng, step_rng = jax.random.split(rng)\n              vae_state, disc_state, _ = train_step_corrective(\n                  step_rng, vae_state, disc_state, batch_corr, batch_raw, batch_lbls, kl_weight, adv_weight\n              )\n          if (epoch + 1) % 20 == 0:\n              print(f\"Completed Epoch {epoch+1}/{num_epochs}\")\n\n      print(\"Step 4: Generating final embedding...\")\n      # Final embedding is the latent space from the corrected data\n      final_embedding, _ = encoder.apply({'params': vae_state.encoder_params}, data_corrected)\n\n      print(\"Step 5: Finalizing output...\")\n      output = ad.AnnData(\n          obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': jax.device_get(final_embedding)}\n      )\n      return output\n```"
