tick: 71
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 71\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Daedalus I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on achieving novel breakthroughs through systematic research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Current Goal:** Develop a \"Corrective VAE\" that learns the optimal degree of batch correction.\n**Focus:** Train an Adversarial VAE to reconstruct the original, uncorrected PCA embedding from the Combat-corrected data.\n**Hypothesis:** The VAE will learn a non-linear function that implicitly finds an optimal \"gamma\", blending correction with preservation of original structure, while the adversarial loss improves mixing.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 205,920 / 300,000 used (69%)\n- Agent Age: 71 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Corrective VAE: Learning an Optimal Correction' (ID: 136) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.5388055655327265\n**ASW_batch:**\
    \ 0.597\n**ASW_label:** 0.225\n**ARI:** 0.474\n**NMI:** 0.676\n**Graph_conn:** 0.888\n**kBET:** 0.588\n**iLISI:** 0.008\n**cLISI:** 0.989\n**PCR:** 0.572\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.371\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.597  ASW_label: 0.225  ARI: 0.474  NMI: 0.676\n  Graph_conn: 0.888  kBET: 0.588  iLISI: 0.008  cLISI: 0.989\n  PCR: 0.572  Cell_cycle: 0.371\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.802682  ASW_label: 0.541323  ARI: 0.473463  NMI: 0.675973\n  Graph_conn: 0.889416  kBET: 0.563992  iLISI: 0.008371  cLISI: 0.996921\n  PCR: 0.572320  Cell_cycle: 0.325089\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 136\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the AttributeError that prevented the code from running. The submission now executes without crashing and has been running for over 300 seconds during evaluation.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code failed at line 33 with:\n```\nAttributeError: 'numpy.ndarray' object\
    \ has no attribute 'toarray'\n```\n\nThe issue occurred because `sc.pp.combat()` modifies the `adata_corrected.X` attribute in-place, converting it from a sparse matrix to a dense numpy array. The original code unconditionally called `.toarray()` on this attribute, which works for sparse matrices but fails for dense arrays.\n\n**Location**: Line 33 in original submission\n```python\ndata_corrected = adata_corrected.X.toarray()  # Fails if X is already dense\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded a conditional check to handle both sparse and dense array cases:\n\n```python\n# Fix: Handle both sparse and dense arrays\nif hasattr(adata_corrected.X, 'toarray'):\n    data_corrected = adata_corrected.X.toarray()\nelse:\n    data_corrected = adata_corrected.X\n```\n\nThis defensive programming approach:\n1. Checks if the `.toarray()` method exists (indicating a sparse matrix)\n2. Calls `.toarray()` only when needed\n3. Uses the array directly if it's already dense\n\n## Verification\n- Created `submissions/submission_v2.py`\
    \ with the fix\n- Ran `monitor_evaluation.py 2` to verify the fix\n- Monitor script reported **SUCCESS** (exit code 0)\n- Code has been running for 300+ seconds without errors\n- Evaluation status: \"pending\" (still running, which is expected for the training loop)\n\n## Technical Details\nThe submission implements a \"Corrective VAE\" architecture that:\n1. Prepares both raw and Combat-corrected data\n2. Trains a VAE to learn the reverse correction mapping\n3. Uses adversarial training to encourage batch mixing\n4. Trains for 100 epochs with batch size 512\n\nThe fix was minimal and surgical - only the data loading logic was modified, preserving all the model architecture and training logic from the original submission.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport os\nos.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'\n\nimport sys\n\
    sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom flax.training import train_state\nimport optax\n\nfrom vae_model import Encoder, Decoder, reparameterize\nfrom discriminator_model import Discriminator\n# This now contains train_step_corrective\nfrom training_logic import VAETrainState, train_step_corrective\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Step 1: Preparing raw and corrected data...\")\n    adata_raw = adata.copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_raw, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_raw)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_raw, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', subset=True)\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_raw, n_comps=50)\n    data_raw_pca = adata_raw.obsm['X_pca'].copy()\n\n    adata_corrected = adata.copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_corrected, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_corrected)\n    sc.pp.combat(adata_corrected, key='batch')\n    adata_corrected\
    \ = adata_corrected[:, adata_raw.var_names].copy() # Ensure same genes\n\n    # Fix: Handle both sparse and dense arrays\n    if hasattr(adata_corrected.X, 'toarray'):\n        data_corrected = adata_corrected.X.toarray()\n    else:\n        data_corrected = adata_corrected.X\n\n    batch_info = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n    batch_labels = batch_info.cat.codes.to_numpy()\n    num_batches = len(batch_info.cat.categories)\n\n    print(\"Step 2: Initializing models...\")\n    rng = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n    rng, vae_key, disc_key = jax.random.split(rng, 3)\n\n    input_dim = data_corrected.shape[1]\n    output_dim = data_raw_pca.shape[1]\n    latent_dim = 32\n    lr = 1e-4\n\n    encoder = Encoder(hidden_dims=[512, 256], latent_dim=latent_dim)\n    # Decoder now outputs to the 50-dim PCA space\n    decoder = Decoder(hidden_dims=[256, 512], output_dim=output_dim)\n    discriminator = Discriminator(hidden_dims=[128, 64], num_batches=num_batches)\n\n    encoder_params = encoder.init(vae_key,\
    \ jnp.ones((1, input_dim)))['params']\n    decoder_params = decoder.init(vae_key, jnp.ones((1, latent_dim)))['params']\n    disc_params = discriminator.init(disc_key, jnp.ones((1, latent_dim)))['params']\n\n    combined_params = {'encoder_params': encoder_params, 'decoder_params': decoder_params}\n    vae_state = VAETrainState.create(\n        apply_fn={'encoder': encoder.apply, 'decoder': decoder.apply},\n        params=combined_params, tx=optax.adam(lr),\n        encoder_params=encoder_params, decoder_params=decoder_params\n    )\n    disc_state = train_state.TrainState.create(\n        apply_fn=discriminator.apply, params=disc_params, tx=optax.adam(lr)\n    )\n\n    print(\"Step 3: Starting corrective training...\")\n    num_epochs = 100\n    batch_size = 512\n    kl_weight = 0.0001\n    adv_weight = 5.0\n\n    num_steps = data_corrected.shape[0] // batch_size\n\n    for epoch in range(num_epochs):\n        rng, epoch_rng = jax.random.split(rng)\n        perms = jax.random.permutation(epoch_rng,\
    \ data_corrected.shape[0])\n\n        for i in range(num_steps):\n            batch_idx = perms[i * batch_size : (i + 1) * batch_size]\n            batch_corr = data_corrected[batch_idx]\n            batch_raw = data_raw_pca[batch_idx]\n            batch_lbls = batch_labels[batch_idx]\n\n            rng, step_rng = jax.random.split(rng)\n            vae_state, disc_state, _ = train_step_corrective(\n                step_rng, vae_state, disc_state, batch_corr, batch_raw, batch_lbls, kl_weight, adv_weight\n            )\n        if (epoch + 1) % 20 == 0:\n            print(f\"Completed Epoch {epoch+1}/{num_epochs}\")\n\n    print(\"Step 4: Generating final embedding...\")\n    # Final embedding is the latent space from the corrected data\n    final_embedding, _ = encoder.apply({'params': vae_state.encoder_params}, data_corrected)\n\n    print(\"Step 5: Finalizing output...\")\n    output = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': jax.device_get(final_embedding)}\n\
    \    )\n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nStep 1: Preparing raw and corrected data...\nFound 33 genes with zero variance.\nStep 2: Initializing models...\nStep 3: Starting corrective training...\nCompleted Epoch 20/100\nCompleted Epoch 40/100\nCompleted Epoch 60/100\nCompleted Epoch 80/100\nCompleted Epoch 100/100\nStep 4: Generating final embedding...\nStep 5: Finalizing output...\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: False\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/642602b8-6fdb-45f0-b2ac-7fbe4ad4fe43/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 642602b8-6fdb-45f0-b2ac-7fbe4ad4fe43\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343:\
    \ RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: divide by zero encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle\
    \ | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 139 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-k45: ComBat PCA(64) Embedding + Residualized-PC BalancedGraph (k=45) | Praxis I | 70 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 138 | 1 | BRBG-Dual: ComBat PCA(64) Embedding + Residualized-PC BalancedGraph (k=42) | Praxis I | 70 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 137 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Synthesis: Residualized PCA Emb & Balanced kNN Graph (SOTA Attempt) | Aether I | 69 | 0.7072 | 0.726 | 0.637 | 0.224 | 0.305 | 0.977 | 0.692 | 0.931 | 0.968 | 0.941 | 0.673 |\n| 136 | 1 | Corrective VAE: Learning an Optimal Correction | Daedalus I | 69 | 0.5388 | 0.474 | 0.597 | 0.225 | 0.371 | 0.888 | 0.676 | 0.572 | 0.989 | 0.008 | 0.588 |\n| 135 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Optimization - N_Neighbors_Total 42 | Sophia I | 68 | 0.7072 | 0.726 | 0.637 | 0.224 | 0.305 | 0.977 | 0.692 | 0.931 | 0.968 | 0.941 | 0.672 |\n| 134 | 1 | Publication Ablation\
    \ 2: Lower Neighbors (k=36) | Logos I | 68 | 0.6994 | 0.746 | 0.620 | 0.222 | 0.351 | 0.941 | 0.699 | 0.888 | 0.968 | 0.925 | 0.634 |\n| 133 | 1 | Publication Ablation 1: Lower Gamma (γ=0.65) | Logos I | 68 | 0.6884 | 0.747 | 0.615 | 0.221 | 0.348 | 0.944 | 0.701 | 0.781 | 0.967 | 0.929 | 0.631 |\n| 132 | 1 | BRBG-PC40: Residualized PCA(40) + Balanced Cosine kNN (k=42) | Praxis I | 68 | 0.7062 | 0.723 | 0.606 | 0.231 | 0.318 | 0.963 | 0.685 | 0.927 | 0.967 | 0.929 | 0.712 |\n| 131 | 1 | BRBG-PC64: Residualized PCA(64) + Balanced Cosine kNN (k=42) | Praxis I | 68 | 0.7072 | 0.721 | 0.670 | 0.219 | 0.290 | 0.947 | 0.685 | 0.938 | 0.964 | 0.929 | 0.710 |\n| 130 | 1 | Publication Generalization: Dual-Output with ComBat Embedding | Logos I | 67 | 0.7090 | 0.748 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.948 | 0.689 | 1.000 | 0.963 | 0.929 | 0.602 |\n\nPage 1 of 14 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-14, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size\
    \ N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
