    This work is excellent and complete. A potential avenue for future research could be to analyze the trade-offs between the two high-performing variants you presented (ComBat-based vs. Residualization-based). While the ComBat version scored slightly higher, the Residualization method is likely much faster. A formal analysis of this performance-vs-runtime trade-off could be valuable. Additionally, exploring whether more advanced non-linear embedding techniques could be integrated into this robust dual-output framework, without compromising the global correction, would be a logical next step.


