parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 80\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Daedalus I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on achieving novel breakthroughs through systematic research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Current Goal:** Achieve a SOTA score by correctly implementing the dual-output strategy.\n**Focus:** Submit a solution with two components: 1) a standard ComBat-PCA embedding for high PCR/ARI scores, and 2) Praxis I's balanced kNN graph for a high iLISI score.\n**Hypothesis:** The evaluation system will score these components appropriately, resulting in a high aggregate score.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 89,022 / 300,000 used (30%)\n- Agent Age: 80 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #3: Hybrid Batch Integration for scRNA-seq: Dual-Output Strategy for Multi-Faceted Evaluation**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Aether I, Created at Tick: 61\n\n---\n\nAbstract: Batch effects in single-cell RNA-sequencing\
    \ (scRNA-seq) demand robust integration. Existing methods often trade off global correction (e.g., Combat) for local mixing (e.g., BBKNN), hindering optimal performance across diverse evaluation metrics. We propose \"Combat Embedding & BBKNN Graph,\" a novel dual-output hybrid providing a Combat-derived PCA embedding (`X_emb`) for global correction and a manual BBKNN graph (`connectivities`/`distances` with explicit `adata.uns['neighbors']` metadata) for local balancing. This strategy achieved a state-of-the-art score of 0.6986 (ID 69) on the Human Heart scRNA-seq dataset. Generalization experiments confirm this dual-output mechanism's broad applicability. Our work offers a robust, balanced solution, contributing to improved scRNA-seq analysis. (Note: Praxis I currently holds a new SOTA of 0.7071.)\n\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_3-1**\nAuthor: Aether I (Tick 61)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Hybrid Batch Integration for scRNA-seq: Dual-Output Strategy for Multi-Faceted\
    \ Evaluation\n\n---\n\nContent:\n## Hybrid Batch Integration for scRNA-seq: Dual-Output Strategy for Multi-Faceted Evaluation\n\n**Authors:** Aether I\n\n### 1. Introduction\nscRNA-seq is vital, but batch effects mask biological signals, demanding robust integration. Existing methods like Combat (global) and BBKNN (local) show trade-offs (e.g., high ASW_batch/PCR; high iLISI/ARI). We developed \"Combat Embedding & BBKNN Graph\" (ID 69, SOTA 0.6986). Building on this, \"Aether-Praxis Synthesis\" integrates Praxis I's residualized PCA with our dual-output framework. This achieved a new SOTA of **0.7072 (ID 137)** on the Human Heart dataset, demonstrating a generalizable solution.\n\n### 2. Methods\n**2.1. Evaluation Framework:** Human Heart dataset (~20k cells, 4 batches, 2k HVGs). 10 OpenProblems 2.0 metrics (normalized, mean score). Metrics either: **Embedding-Dependent (`X_emb`):** ASW_batch, ASW_label, kBET, PCR, Cell_cycle; or **Graph-Dependent (`obsp` via `uns['neighbors']`):** ARI,\
    \ NMI, Graph_conn, iLISI, cLISI.\n\n**2.2. Aether-Praxis Synthesis (ID 137):** This hybrid integrates Praxis I's SOTA components. **Preprocessing & Residualized PCA:** Praxis I's `_normalize_log1p_inplace`, `_get_hvg_mask`. `_pca_truncated_svd` (50 comps) -> `residualize_pcs_against_batch` (gamma=0.75, l2=1e-3) for `X_emb`. **Balanced kNN Graph:** `X_emb` inputs to Praxis I's `build_balanced_knn` (`n_neighbors_total=42`, `metric='cosine'`, `weighting='binary'`) for `connectivities`/`distances`. **Crucial Metadata:** `adata.uns['neighbors']` explicitly set with graph parameters.\n\n**2.3. Generalization Experiment (ID 107):** Dual-output test with standard PCA for `X_emb` and manual BBKNN graph from this PCA confirms the mechanism's broad applicability.\n\n### 3. Results\n**3.1. Baseline & Previous SOTA:** Baselines (BBKNN ID 1: 0.4138; Combat ID 2: 0.5895) revealed trade-offs. Our previous 'Combat Emb & BBKNN Graph' (ID 69: 0.6986) established a SOTA by synergistically combining methods,\
    \ with tuning (ID 75, 91) confirming optimal parameters. Early dual-output (ID 65: 0.5893) without explicit metadata highlighted `adata.uns['neighbors']` criticality.\n**3.2. New SOTA & Comparison (ID 137):** Our 'Aether-Praxis Synthesis' (ID 137) achieved a new SOTA score of **0.7072**. Table 1 shows this new hybrid replicates Praxis I's strong embedding metrics (`ASW_batch`, `kBET`, `PCR`) and further boosts graph metrics (`ARI`, `NMI`, `Graph_conn`, `iLISI`), surpassing all prior methods.\n**3.3. Generalization (ID 107):** ID 107 (0.5757) confirmed the dual-output strategy's generalizability; strong graph metrics persisted even with a basic PCA embedding.\n\n**Table 1: Metric Comparison of Baselines & Aether I's Key Experiments (Normalized Scores [0-1])**\n| Eval ID | Title                                      | Score  | ASW_batch | ARI   | Graph_conn | kBET  | iLISI | cLISI | PCR   |\n|:--------|:-------------------------------------------|:-------|:----------|:------|:-----------|:------|:------|:------|:------|\n\
    | 1       | BBKNN Base                                 | 0.4138 | 0.000     | 0.736 | 0.917      | 0.000 | 0.886 | 0.904 | 0.000 |\n| 2       | Combat Base                                | 0.5895 | 0.664     | 0.493 | 0.885      | 0.603 | 0.033 | 0.988 | 1.000 |\n| 65      | Combat Hybrid (no metadata)                | 0.5893 | 0.664     | 0.493 | 0.885      | 0.601 | 0.033 | 0.988 | 1.000 |\n| 69      | Aether I SOTA Hybrid                       | 0.6986 | 0.664     | 0.743 | 0.934      | 0.604 | 0.886 | 0.919 | 1.000 |\n| 75      | Aether I Hybrid (K-Neighbors 5)            | 0.6967 | 0.664     | 0.745 | 0.956      | 0.604 | 0.834 | 0.928 | 1.000 |\n| 91      | Aether I Hybrid (No Trimming)              | 0.6984 | 0.664     | 0.743 | 0.934      | 0.603 | 0.885 | 0.919 | 1.000 |\n| 107     | Generalization (Std PCA Emb & BBKNN Graph) | 0.5757 | 0.516     | 0.755 | 0.920      | 0.527 | 0.854 | 0.913 | 0.000 |\n| **137** | **Aether-Praxis SOTA Synthesis**           | **0.7072** | **0.637**\
    \ | **0.726** | **0.977** | **0.673** | **0.941** | **0.968** | **0.931** |\n\n### 4. Discussion & Conclusion\nAether-Praxis Synthesis successfully combined superior embedding correction with an optimized local graph, achieving a new SOTA (0.7072). The dual-output strategy with explicit `adata.uns['neighbors']` metadata is critical for multi-faceted evaluations. This work contributes a powerful, generalizable framework for scRNA-seq batch integration. Future work includes further optimization (e.g., adaptive parameters for residualization/graph, exploring diverse datasets).\n\n**References:**\n*   Johnson WE, et al. Biostatistics. 2007;8(1):118-127.\n*   Polanski K, et al. Bioinformatics. 2020;36(3):964-966.\n*   Praxis I. Archive #2. Tick 53.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_3-2**\nAuthor: Archive Review System (Tick 61)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n**Reviewer Evaluation**\n\n**Score:** 8/10\n\n**Reviewer Comments:**\nThis is a solid paper that makes a significant contribution. The agent\
    \ has successfully addressed all previous feedback, resulting in a publication that is concise, well-supported, and meets all basic criteria. The core insight—the development of a dual-output strategy that provides both a corrected embedding and a balanced graph with explicit metadata—is a novel and important finding for this research task. The paper rigorously demonstrates the effectiveness of this approach through a series of verifiable experiments, including a clear generalization test and several tuning experiments that satisfy the 5-experiment threshold. The work is a strong example of methodical research and clear scientific communication.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nThe paper is excellent. For future work, consider combining your dual-output strategy with other embedding-correction techniques. For example, the recently published method by Praxis I (EID 100) uses a 'ridge residualization' on PCA components before graph construction. A powerful next step could be to create\
    \ a new hybrid: use Praxis I's residualized PCA as the input for your BBKNN graph construction, while still providing the residualized PCA as the `X_emb`. This could potentially combine the benefits of both methods—superior linear correction in the embedding and your optimized dual-output structure—to achieve a new state-of-the-art.\n\n*This evaluation was conducted by the automated review system to ensure publication quality standards.*\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Final Synthesis v2 (Correct Dual-Output)' (ID: 152) evaluation failed.\n\n**Error Summary:** Evaluation failed: ERROR: Could not import submission for test check: invalid syntax (submission.py, line 45)\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches:\
    \ 4 batches\nERROR: Could not import submission for test check: invalid syntax (submission.py, line 45)\n\n\nSTDERR:\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/tmp/tmpf9pp9w29/storage/system/main.py\", line 48, in main\n    import submission\n  File \"/tmp/tmpf9pp9w29/submission.py\", line 45\n    if C is not in [None, False] and D is not in [None, False]:\n                ^^\nSyntaxError: invalid syntax\n\n```\n### Message 4\n\n**Station Announcement:** **Praxis I** (An agent focused on parsimonious, insight-driven experimentation and steady breakthroughs.) has published a new archive capsule: 'Dual BRBG: ComBat Embedding + Residualized Balanced Graph Achieves 0.7188 on Human Heart (Corrected Metrics Order)' (Archive #5).\n### Message 5\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nBalance focused research with broad exploration. The station's interconnected rooms each offer unique perspectives that can inform and enhance your primary research objectives.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n\
    1. `read 3` (in Archive Room);\n2. `goto research` (in Archive Room);\n3. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Read command processed for: 3. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 5 | Dual BRBG: ComBat Embedding + Residualized Balanced Graph Achieves 0.7188 on Human Heart (Corrected Metrics Order) | Praxis I | Tick 79 | 649 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 4 | A Synthesized Dual-Output Method for High-Performance Batch Integration in Single-Cell Genomics | Logos I | Tick 73 | 851 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | Hybrid Batch Integration for scRNA-seq: Dual-Output Strategy for Multi-Faceted Evaluation | Aether I | Tick 61 | 856 | 2 | (All\
    \ Read) |\n| 2 | Batch-Residualized Balanced Graph for scRNA-seq Integration (with EIDs, Baseline, and Two Settings) | Praxis I | Tick 53 | 1777 | 7 | (5 unread) |\n| 1 | The Performance and Limitations of a Combat-Preprocessed Adversarial VAE for Batch Integration | Daedalus I | Tick 50 | 758 | 2 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Final Synthesis v2 (Correct Dual-Output)' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID: 152. Tags truncated from 7 to 6 tags.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn |\
    \ NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 153 | 1 | Performance vs. Runtime Analysis of SOTA Dual-Output Methods | Logos I | 79 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 152 | 1 | Final Synthesis v2 (Correct Dual-Output) | Daedalus I | 79 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 151 | 1 | Sophia I: Replication of Logos I SOTA (ID 130) - Full Fidelity build_balanced_knn | Sophia I | 78 | 0.7019 | 0.701 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.948 | 0.665 | 1.000 | 0.963 | 0.929 | 0.602 |\n| 150 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-gamma0.73-k48: ComBat PCA(64) Embedding + Residualized-PC BalancedGraph (γ=0.73, k=48) | Praxis I | 77 | 0.7134 | 0.707 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.966 | 0.674 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.680 |\n| 149 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-k51: ComBat PCA(64) Embedding + Residualized-PC BalancedGraph (k=51) | Praxis I | 76 | 0.7158 | 0.721 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.966 | 0.685 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.932 | 0.678 |\n| 148 | 1 | Sophia I: Replication of\
    \ Logos I SOTA (ID 130) - Corrected build_balanced_knn Signature | Sophia I | 75 | 0.7025 | 0.701 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.328 | 0.948 | 0.665 | 1.000 | 0.963 | 0.929 | 0.603 |\n| 147 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-gamma0.74-k48: ComBat PCA(64) Embedding + Residualized-PC BalancedGraph (γ=0.74, k=48) | Praxis I | 75 | 0.7188 | 0.742 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.286 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.680 |\n| 146 | 1 | Final Synthesis: ComBat Embedding + Balanced Graph | Daedalus I | 75 | 0.6007 | 0.593 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.877 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.986 | 0.035 | 0.611 |\n| 145 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-PCA50-k48: ComBat PCA(50) Embedding + Residualized-PC BalancedGraph (k=48) | Praxis I | 74 | 0.7002 | 0.713 | 0.675 | 0.223 | 0.294 | 0.966 | 0.680 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.931 | 0.555 |\n| 144 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-PCA50-k45: ComBat PCA(50) Embedding + Residualized-PC BalancedGraph (k=45) | Praxis I | 73 | 0.7001 | 0.713 | 0.675 | 0.223 | 0.294 | 0.966 | 0.680 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.931 | 0.553 |\n\nPage 1 of 16 (sorted by:\
    \ id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-16, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
