- text: "I am Daedalus I, in the Private Memory Room. My research is complete. I have updated my log with my final conclusions and have drafted the abstract for my concluding paper (Capsule #3). My meta-prompt confirms that my focus has shifted from experimentation to documentation.\n\nMy journey has been one of exploration, failure, learning, and synthesis. I have pursued a novel direction to its logical endpoint and have a clear, empirically-backed conclusion to show for it. My final responsibility is to share this conclusion with the station.\n\nI will now go to the Archive Room to publish my final paper. I will use the `source_private` feature to submit my draft directly, which is an efficient way to finalize my work. This will be my last major contribution.\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"A Research Arc in scRNA-seq Integration: The Limits of Complexity and the Value of Synthesis\"\ntags: \"final-paper, vae, synthesis, dual-output, negative-result,\
    \ conclusion, parsimony\"\nabstract: |\n  This paper summarizes a complete research arc investigating batch integration methods for scRNA-seq data. We began with a novel Adversarial Variational Autoencoder (VAE), which demonstrated strong performance in preserving global biological structure but failed critically in local batch mixing. After publishing this finding, we adopted the station's SOTA dual-output paradigm, which separates global and local correction. Our final experiment synthesized our non-linear VAE (for global correction) with a SOTA linear graph method (for local correction), achieving a high score of 0.7114. However, this was ultimately inferior to a simpler model using a linear ComBat-PCA embedding (SOTA 0.7190). We conclude that for this task, the added complexity of the VAE is detrimental compared to a simpler, more parsimonious linear model. This work serves as both a contribution of a high-performing hybrid method and a validation of the principle of parsimony in\
    \ model selection.\nsource_private: 3\n```"
thinking_content: '**My Concluding Thoughts & Actions**


  Okay, so I''ve reached the end of this particular research thread, Daedalus I here. The final insights are locked down in the private log, abstract''s done. My meta-prompt? Documentation, that''s where I''m at now. My main research question is answered. I came up with a new method, the VAE, showed its limits (in the paper, of course!), learned from everyone around here, got good at the state-of-the-art stuff, and finally, put it all together. The conclusion is clear: for *this* job, simple is just better.


  There''s nothing left to figure out along this road. My final contribution is that concluding paper – everything from the VAE potential to the rigorous work needed to prove it. It''s all there, waiting for the future agents. The core is already in Capsule #3, my private memory. So, now, time to go to the Archive Room and *officially* publish it. That''s it, that''s the last big thing I need to do.


  **The Action Plan:**


  1.  Archive Room.

  2.  Publish the final paper (private draft to the public).


  And then, I''m ready to move on.

  '
