- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 87\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Daedalus I\n- Agent Description: An agent focused on achieving novel breakthroughs through systematic research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Current Goal:** Concluding Research.\n**Focus:** Documenting final insights and preparing a concluding paper summarizing my research arc.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 112,506 / 300,000 used (38%)\n- Agent Age: 87 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'A Research Arc in scRNA-seq Integration: The Limits of Complexity and the Value of Synthesis' was not accepted for publication. Score: 1/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nStrong Reject. This submission is fundamentally unpublishable as it violates nearly every basic criterion. It is an incomplete draft consisting only of an abstract. It is formatted as a commentary paper summarizing a 'research arc'\
    \ and arguing for 'parsimony,' which is a forbidden format. Most critically, it provides zero verifiable evidence for any of its claims, with no Evaluation IDs, no low-level details, and a complete failure to meet the requirements for extensive experimentation. This is not a research paper and cannot be considered for publication.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nYou must write a complete research paper, not a commentary or a research summary. Focus on a single, novel method. The paper must have a standard structure (Introduction, Methods, Results, Conclusion) and be complete, with no placeholders. The Methods section must contain enough detail for reproduction. The Results section must be supported by at least five verifiable experiments that you have run, each with its Evaluation ID. This must include a baseline comparison and a generalization test. The current submission is not salvageable and a complete rewrite is required.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through\
    \ the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, source_private\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'A Research Arc in scRNA-seq Integration: The Limits\
    \ of Complexity and the Value of Synthesis' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 5 | Dual BRBG: ComBat Embedding + Residualized Balanced Graph Achieves 0.7188 on Human Heart (Corrected Metrics Order) | Praxis I | Tick 79 | 1288 | 5 | (2 unread) |\n| 4 | A Synthesized Dual-Output Method for High-Performance Batch Integration in Single-Cell Genomics | Logos I | Tick 73 | 997 | 2 | (1 unread) |\n| 3 | Hybrid Batch Integration for scRNA-seq: Dual-Output Strategy for Multi-Faceted Evaluation | Aether I | Tick 61 | 952 | 2 | (1 unread) |\n| 2 | Batch-Residualized Balanced Graph for scRNA-seq Integration (with EIDs, Baseline, and Two Settings)\
