tick: 88
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Daedalus I, in the Research Counter. My meta-prompt correctly reflects my current goal: to conduct the necessary experiments to publish my \"Ultimate Synthesis\" method.\n\nMy first supporting experiment, \"Ablation for Paper: VAE Embedding + Standard Graph\" (ID 160), is currently running. This experiment will provide a crucial point of comparison, demonstrating the value added by the specialized balanced kNN graph over a standard approach.\n\nWhile I wait for the results, I will continue with the required experiments. The next logical step is to establish a clear baseline. My \"Ultimate Synthesis\" (ID 155) combines two components. To justify this synthesis, I must show its performance against a simple, single-component baseline. The best baseline is the ComBat-PCA embedding on its own, with a standard kNN graph built from it for the graph metrics. This is essentially my very first successful experiment (ID 4), but I will run it again to have a clean, contemporary EID for\
    \ the paper.\n\nI will now submit this baseline experiment.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Baseline for Paper: ComBat Embedding + Standard Graph\"\ntags: \"publication-support, baseline, combat, standard-knn\"\nabstract: |\n  This is a required baseline experiment for my upcoming paper on the \"Ultimate Synthesis\" method (ID 155). It evaluates the performance of a simple, single-component approach: a ComBat-corrected PCA embedding, with a standard kNN graph built from that embedding. This will serve as the primary baseline against which the performance of my more complex, dual-component \"Ultimate Synthesis\" method will be compared in the final publication, demonstrating the value of the 'separation of concerns' strategy.\ncontent: |\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # --- Part 1: Generate the ComBat-PCA Embedding ---\n      print(\"Part 1: Generating the ComBat-PCA embedding...\"\
    )\n      adata_proc = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_proc, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_proc)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_proc, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', subset=True)\n      sc.pp.combat(adata_proc, key='batch')\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_proc, n_comps=50)\n\n      # --- Part 2: Build a Standard kNN Graph ---\n      print(\"Part 2: Building a standard kNN graph on the ComBat embedding...\")\n      # The embedding is already in adata_proc.obsm['X_pca']\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata_proc, use_rep='X_pca', n_neighbors=48)\n      \n      # --- Part 3: Finalize Output ---\n      print(\"Part 3: Finalizing output...\")\n      # The `neighbors` function automatically populates .obsp and .uns,\n      # and the embedding is already present. This adata object is complete.\n      return adata_proc\n```"
