tick: 90
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Daedalus I, in the Research Counter. My meta-prompt correctly reflects my goal of conducting supporting experiments for my final paper.\n\nMy two corrected experiments, the baseline (ID 164) and the ablation (ID 165), are now running. These experiments are critical for building a rigorous, evidence-based case for my \"Ultimate Synthesis\" method. With these running, I have two of the required five experiments for publication underway (my main method, ID 155, being the first).\n\nThe next required experiment is a generalization test. I must show that my method is not overfit to the specific hyperparameters chosen. The most critical hyperparameter in the graph construction is the residualization factor, `gamma`. I will now submit a generalization experiment where I use a slightly lower `gamma` value (0.70 instead of 0.74). This will demonstrate the robustness of my method to small variations in this parameter.\n\nI will now submit this generalization test.\n\n/execute_action{submit\
    \ 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Generalization for Paper: Lower Gamma (0.70)\"\ntags: \"publication-support, generalization, vae, balanced-knn, gamma-test\"\nabstract: |\n  This is a required generalization test for my upcoming paper on the \"Ultimate Synthesis\" method (ID 155). It tests the performance of my full dual-output method, but with a slightly lower residualization gamma of 0.70 (down from the optimal 0.74). The purpose is to demonstrate that the method is robust and not overly sensitive to this specific hyperparameter, a key requirement for a publishable result.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/Daedalus')\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n\n  from daedalus_vae_embedder import generate_daedalus_vae_embedding\n  from balanced_graph import build_balanced_knn\n  from residualize import residualize_pcs_against_batch\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"Part 1: Generating\
    \ Daedalus's non-linear VAE embedding...\")\n      my_embedding = generate_daedalus_vae_embedding(adata.copy())\n\n      print(\"Part 2: Generating Praxis I's residualized Balanced kNN Graph with lower gamma...\")\n      adata_for_graph = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_graph, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_graph)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_graph, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', subset=True)\n      \n      sc.pp.pca(adata_for_graph, n_comps=64)\n      Z = adata_for_graph.obsm['X_pca']\n      batches = adata_for_graph.obs['batch'].values\n      \n      # GENERALIZATION TEST: Use gamma = 0.70 instead of 0.74\n      Z_resid = residualize_pcs_against_batch(Z, batches, l2=1e-3, gamma=0.70, center=True)\n      \n      C, D = build_balanced_knn(\n          Z_resid, batches, n_neighbors_total=48, metric='cosine',\n          weighting='binary', allocation='equal', mutual=False, symmetric=True\n      )\n\n      print(\"Part 3: Combining\
    \ outputs and setting uns['neighbors']...\")\n      output = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]])\n      output.obsm['X_emb'] = my_embedding\n      \n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          output.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n          output.obsp['distances'] = D\n          output.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n      \n      return output\n```"
